"""
valgen_core.py — VAL generational model, steps P1 to P5
=======================================================
A family line on a double-entry ledger: four valuation routes, a death every G
years, an heir, declaration strategies, a verification / corrective-auction
hazard, and a search for the best declaration response under each refund rule.
Working name; becomes val_core.py at cutover (plan §8).
Plan: VAL_generational_model_plan.md (v0.7).

P1  run_life():    one life, sale at N, post-sale settlement. Reproduces the
                   legacy results (wdt_core.run_pair / run_sim_hist) to 1e-9.
P2  run_family():  Route C only. A family over horizon T with a death every G
                   years and an heir. No sale, no verification (lambda = 0).
                   Switches: heir influx ('delta' D6 | 'fresh_entrant' CLOSE 4.1)
                   and envelope unit ('real' E2 | 'credited' E1).
P2b run_family():  consumption (D16/D17), W_min / k indexing (D16) and the
                   ratio-mirror refund (D8), all off by default.
                   refund_rule   'legacy'       refund = tau x delta / W_new, capped by
                                                the credited / real envelope (bridge only).
                                 'ratio_mirror' refund fraction of holdings
                                                = tau x (1 - W_new / W_prev), the mirror of
                                                the payment fraction. In units, capped by
                                                the units this individual has paid.
P3  run_family3(): four routes A/B/C/D (D1-D3, D7, D13, D21), see the P3 header. A LEDGER WRAPPER over
                   wdt_kernel (the shared settlement kernel, D12): the kernel does the route arithmetic, _LedgerHook posts
                   it. Independent hazards lambda_C (verify_hazard) and lambda_D (verify_hazard_D). Route D reset is a
                   strategy action (reset=), not a schedule; the scheduled reset_interval and death_waiver are RETIRED
                   (run_family3 raises TypeError on them). Death always auctions Route D. Route B modes sale/lien/income.
                   run_batch() runs many strategy lines through one kernel call (parity with run_family3 ~1e-15).
P4  run_family3(verify_hazard=lambda): expected-value verification of Route C (D9).
P5  run_family3(...) + _p5_search(): declaration strategies, rule switches, and the
                   BRG/HSC/SPT/SST verdicts by rule set and lambda; plus the growth x lambda surface.

CAPS (plan D8, 1 Oct)
---------------------
Route C is paid in kind, so its refund cap is in UNITS (u_out = units this individual
has paid to the state, net of units returned). A/B pay cash-equivalent units and keep
the pooled real-value envelope (E2). The two caps are separate. c_cap='units_and_value'
adds the real-value cap to Route C as well (without it Route C can refund several times
the value paid, because returned units carry the growth since payment).

RULE SETS (P5)
--------------
Fixed in every run (decisions of 1-3 Oct): ratio-mirror Route C refund (D8), free entry
basis, L allocated by delta shares (D21), Route D write-down refund symmetric, D7 netting.
A rule set is a key 'c_cap/verify_down/dauc', trailing parts optional (see _p5_opts):
    c_cap        units | units_and_value  Route C refund cap (value cap needed: units alone
                                          refunds up to ~4x the value paid)
    verify_down  allow | reset            reset = correcting your own overstatement at
                                          verification / auction is a basis reset with no
                                          refund (VAL 11.3, corrective over-declaration)
    dauc         off | on                 corrective auction also applies to Route D
The simple universal candidate is units_and_value/reset/on. The other keys are ablations
that show what each component buys.
Verdicts: BRG best-response gain <= brg_tol; HSC honest family's cost from the rule in a
genuine shock <= hsc_tol; SPT and SST: state PV and stake within state_tol wherever the family gains.

P6  Route B archetypes and breakeven deferral spread.  P7  JST replay (D1a) and rho sensitivity (D1c).
Also: lambda_C x lambda_D grid, V0 sweep over the RATES revenue bands, HLC pair (burdens from the
TOML-held calibration [val_gen.hlc]; skipped, with the reason, while it is a PLACEHOLDER). The legacy bridge now runs on a JST real
return series (UNVERIFIED against the real JST file: only a synthetic series was available).

Not built: heir pre-existing wealth H, route-specific g, gifts (D20), failed assets,
net-accumulation-base metric, a voluntary downward re-declaration that needs an auction.

LAYER
-----
Layer 3 core. Imports wdt_core (base layer) and wdt_fmt (paths) only. It does
NOT import val_core or any other core. It writes
    OUTPUTS/VAL/valgen_data.json
and leaves OUTPUTS/VAL/val_data.json (legacy) untouched; both live in OUTPUTS/VAL/.

LEDGER
------
Accounts hold TRUE (economic) value in £m:
    market          source of growth (balance = -total value created)
    family_equity   family's stake in the asset
    family_cash     family's cash (after the sale)
    state_equity    state's stake (units received as in-kind tax)
    state_cash      state's cash
    consumed        cumulative true value consumed (units sold to the market)
Every post() moves value from one account to another, so the sum of all
balances is zero by construction. The checks that bite are:
  (a) family_equity == f * V each year (in-kind identity true_paid = L / alpha).
  (b) f + s + sold == 1 (units; sold = cumulative units consumed).
  (c) family_total + state_total == (1 - sold) * V.
  (d) 0 <= u_out <= s (refundable units never exceed the state's stake).
  (e) the bridge to legacy (P1).

METRICS (same sign conventions as wdt_core.run_pair)
----------------------------------------------------
  net_pct  (Net(a) - Net(1)) / TW(1)       + = pays more net tax
  tw_gap   (TW(a)  - TW(1))  / TW(1)       + = retains more
  pv_pct   (PV(a)  - PV(1))  / TW(1)       + = pays more in PV
  pv_rel   (PV(a)  - PV(1))  / PV(1)       None where PV(1) < pv_rel_min_frac * TW(1)
SPT/SST (plan §2): the state is "within tolerance" when |pv_rel| <= state_tol
(two-sided, fraction of honest PV tax revenue; [val_gen] state_tol).

LEGACY DEVICE KEPT FOR THE BRIDGE ONLY
--------------------------------------
_settle_post_sale-style iteration in run_life() exists so P1 can match legacy
TW_settled / Net_settled. In the family engine the heir's years run explicitly;
check 7 (_oscillation_check) shows the explicit annual flows reproduce the
legacy settle_tw_flows net tax.

Usage
-----
    python valgen_core.py             # run bridge + validation, write JSON
    python valgen_core.py --dry-run   # print grid sizes only
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import json
import math
import sys
from datetime import date

import sys
from pathlib import Path
sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))   # model root: wdt_core, wdt_fmt, wdt_md, wdt_style

import numpy as np

import wdt_kernel as wk                    # the shared route-settlement kernel (D12)
from wdt_core import scenario_medians, load_params, tau, simulate, run_pair, run_sim_hist, settle_tw_flows, rate_params, rate_vec, with_rate_scenario, with_val_basis, BASIS_CONVENTION, load_json
from wdt_fmt import out_dir, ensure_dir
from wdt_jst import loop_windows, load_jst, real_return_series   # D1a / D1b

_OUT = out_dir('VAL')
_JSON_PATH = _OUT / 'valgen_data.json'

# ── numerical constants (not model inputs) ────────────────────
BRIDGE_TOL     = 1e-9    # pure-move discipline (plan §7 check 2)
CONSERVE_TOL   = 1e-9    # relative to V
SETTLE_MAX_ITER = 2000   # as legacy settle_tw_flows
SETTLE_TOL     = 1e-10   # as legacy settle_tw_flows

# Regression fixtures from plan §1 (no verification ever; single life, no sale;
# family stake vs honest). Rounded as quoted in the plan, so compared to 0.5pp.
# Keys: (N, alpha) -> gain. They are test fixtures, not model inputs.
PLAN_S1_GAIN = {(30, 0.1): 0.031, (30, 0.5): 0.017,           # derived on the POST-settlement basis (11 Oct 2026):
                (90, 0.1): 2.818, (90, 0.5): 0.546, (90, 2.0): -0.356, (90, 5.0): -0.64}   # a regression guard, not an outside check
PLAN_S1_TOL  = 0.005
# Plan §1: flat rate, no threshold -> family stake identical for every alpha.
# Value quoted 0.685117 at N = 30 (plan v0.7 corrects the row label).
PLAN_S1_FLAT_N, PLAN_S1_FLAT_STAKE = 30, 0.651285   # post basis; hand value (1 - tau g/(1+g))^30

# The fixtures above hold only at the baseline calibration: they are regression tests for THAT calibration.
# At other rate parameters, V0_m or g they are skipped (and the UCC benchmark is flagged), not failed.
PLAN_S1_BASELINE = {'tau_0': 0.15, 'tau_m': 0.70, 'k': 0.001, 'W_min': 2.0, 'V0_m': 20.0, 'g_real': 0.1045}


def _ir(p: dict) -> float:
    """W_min / k index rate: p['index_rate'] (set by wdt_core.with_val_basis) else the legacy [budget] budget_growth."""
    return p.get('index_rate', p['budget_growth'])


def _plan_fixture_applies(p: dict, keys=None) -> bool:
    """True when the parameters the fixtures depend on equal the baseline (all of them, or just `keys`)."""
    if keys is None and p.get('schedule', 'logistic') != 'logistic':
        return False                      # the fixtures are for the baseline logistic only
    return all(abs(p[k] - PLAN_S1_BASELINE[k]) < 1e-12 for k in (keys or PLAN_S1_BASELINE))


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEDGER
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

_ACCOUNTS = ('market', 'family_equity', 'family_cash', 'state_equity', 'state_cash', 'consumed')


class Ledger:
    """Double-entry ledger in true £m. post() moves value src -> dst."""

    def __init__(self, accounts=_ACCOUNTS):
        self.bal = dict.fromkeys(accounts, 0.0)
        self.entries: list[dict] = []

    def post(self, t, kind, src, dst, amount, **memo):
        """Move `amount` from src to dst; a negative amount reverses direction."""
        if amount < 0.0:
            src, dst, amount = dst, src, -amount
        self.bal[src] -= amount
        self.bal[dst] += amount
        self.entries.append({'t': t, 'kind': kind, 'src': src, 'dst': dst,
                             'amount': amount, **memo})

    def family_total(self):
        return self.bal['family_equity'] + self.bal['family_cash']

    def state_total(self):
        return self.bal['state_equity'] + self.bal['state_cash']


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE ASSESSMENT RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

_ENVELOPE_UNITS = ('real', 'credited')
_HEIR_RULES     = ('delta', 'fresh_entrant')
_REFUND_RULES   = ('legacy', 'ratio_mirror')


def _assess(W_new, W_prev, cap, sim_p):
    """
    Legacy assessment on total declared wealth (plan D7), used by P1's sale and
    post-sale settlement.

        delta = W_new - W_prev
        L     = max(-cap, tau(W_new) * delta)   if delta > 0 or cap > 0
              = 0                               otherwise
    `cap` is the refund envelope in CREDITED pounds. Returns (L, rate, delta).
    """
    rate  = tau(W_new, sim_p)
    delta = W_new - W_prev
    L     = max(-cap, rate * delta) if (delta > 0.0 or cap > 0.0) else 0.0
    return L, rate, delta


def _new_state(alpha, V0):
    """Route C holder: f family units, s state units, W last declared, envelopes."""
    return {'f': 1.0, 's': 0.0, 'W': alpha * V0, 'cum': 0.0, 'cum_true': 0.0,
            'u_out': 0.0, 'sold': 0.0}


def _cap(st, alpha, envelope_unit):
    """Legacy refund envelope in credited pounds (see _assess)."""
    return st['cum'] if envelope_unit == 'credited' else alpha * st['cum_true']


def _assess_c(st, W_new, W_prev, alpha, sim_p, idx, envelope_unit, rule):
    """
    Route C assessment. Returns (q, L, rate, delta): q is the signed fraction of
    the holder's units that moves (+ = family -> state), L the credited pounds
    (= q x W_new). The rate is tau(W_new / idx): W_min and k indexed together.

    'legacy'        q = L / W_new, L as in _assess (credited / real envelope).
    'ratio_mirror'  delta > 0: q = tau x delta / W_new = tau (1 - W_prev / W_new).
                    delta < 0: q = -tau (1 - W_new / W_prev), floored at
                    -u_out / f, i.e. the family can never get back more units
                    than it has paid.
    """
    rate  = tau(W_new / idx, sim_p)
    delta = W_new - W_prev
    if rule == 'legacy':
        cap = _cap(st, alpha, envelope_unit)
        L   = max(-cap, rate * delta) if (delta > 0.0 or cap > 0.0) else 0.0
        q   = (L / W_new) if W_new != 0.0 else 0.0
        return q, L, rate, delta
    if delta > 0.0:
        L = rate * delta
        return (L / W_new), L, rate, delta
    if delta < 0.0 and st['u_out'] > 0.0 and st['f'] > 0.0 and W_prev > 0.0:
        q = max(-rate * (1.0 - W_new / W_prev), -st['u_out'] / st['f'])
        return q, q * W_new, rate, delta
    return 0.0, 0.0, rate, delta


def _check(led, st, V_now, diag, units_held=True):
    """Ledger invariants. Updates the running worst-case in diag."""
    diag['unit_err'] = max(diag['unit_err'],
                           abs(led.bal['family_equity'] - st['f'] * V_now) / V_now)
    sold = st.get('sold', 0.0)
    if units_held:
        diag['cons_err'] = max(diag['cons_err'], abs(st['f'] + st['s'] + sold - 1.0))
        expect = V_now * (1.0 - sold)
    else:
        expect = V_now * (1.0 - sold)
    diag['cons_err'] = max(diag['cons_err'],
                           abs(led.family_total() + led.state_total() - expect) / V_now)
    diag['uout_err'] = max(diag['uout_err'], st['u_out'] - st['s'], -st['u_out'], 0.0)
    diag['min_state_units'] = min(diag['min_state_units'], st['s'])
    diag['min_state_cash']  = min(diag['min_state_cash'], led.bal['state_cash'])


def _new_diag():
    return {'cons_err': 0.0, 'unit_err': 0.0, 'uout_err': 0.0,
            'min_state_units': 0.0, 'min_state_cash': 0.0}


def _pay_in_kind(led, t, kind, st, V, L, q):
    """
    Settle a credited amount L in kind at the declared price: the holder moves
    fraction q of its units to the state (q < 0 is a refund in units from the
    state's stake). Returns (q, true value moved to the state).
    """
    units = st['f'] * q                       # + = family -> state
    paid  = units * V                         # true value (= L / alpha)
    led.post(t, kind, 'family_equity', 'state_equity', paid, credited=L, units=units)
    st['f']        -= units
    st['s']        += units
    st['u_out']    += units
    st['cum']      += L
    st['cum_true'] += paid
    return q, paid


def _holding_year(led, t, st, V_prev, V, alpha, sim_p, envelope_unit,
                  idx=1.0, refund_rule='legacy', c=0.0):
    """
    One annual assessment of a Route C holder. Shared by P1, P2 and P2b.
    Order: growth -> consumption (units sold) -> assessment -> payment in kind.
    Defaults (idx = 1, legacy, c = 0) are the P1/P2 rule exactly.
    """
    led.post(t, 'growth', 'market', 'family_equity', st['f'] * (V - V_prev))
    led.post(t, 'growth', 'market', 'state_equity',  st['s'] * (V - V_prev))
    cons_val = 0.0
    if c > 0.0:
        cu       = st['f'] * c
        cons_val = cu * V
        led.post(t, 'consume', 'family_equity', 'consumed', cons_val, units=cu)
        st['f']    -= cu
        st['sold'] += cu
    W_new = st['f'] * alpha * V
    q, L, rate, delta = _assess_c(st, W_new, st['W'], alpha, sim_p, idx,
                                  envelope_unit, refund_rule)
    q, paid = _pay_in_kind(led, t, 'tax_inkind', st, V, L, q)
    W_new = st['f'] * alpha * V                  # POST-surrender basis (BASIS_CHANGE)
    st['W'] = W_new
    row = {'t': t, 'V': V, 'W': W_new, 'f': st['f'], 's': st['s'], 'cum': st['cum'],
           'L': L, 'rate': rate, 'delta': delta, 'q': q, 'true_paid': paid,
           'consumed': cons_val, 'u_out': st['u_out']}
    return row, (t, 'tax_inkind', paid, L)


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P1 — ONE LIFE, ONE ROUTE, SALE AT N
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def run_life(p: dict, alpha: float, g_series: list, g_sell: float) -> dict:
    """
    Simulate one Route C taxpayer: N holding years, a sale in year N+1,
    post-sale settlement (legacy device). Declared value D_t = alpha * V_t.
    Envelope unit is E1 (credited): the legacy convention the bridge requires.
    """
    sim_p = rate_params(p)
    N     = len(g_series)
    V     = p['V0_m']
    st    = _new_state(alpha, V)
    led   = Ledger()
    receipts: list[tuple] = []   # (t, kind, true value received by state, credited L)
    diag  = _new_diag()

    led.post(0, 'endow', 'market', 'family_equity', V)
    rows = [{'t': 0, 'V': V, 'W': st['W'], 'f': 1.0, 's': 0.0, 'cum': 0.0, 'L': 0.0,
             'rate': tau(st['W'], sim_p), 'delta': 0.0, 'q': 0.0, 'true_paid': 0.0}]
    _check(led, st, V, diag)

    for t in range(1, N + 1):
        V_prev = V
        V      = V * (1.0 + g_series[t - 1])
        row, rc = _holding_year(led, t, st, V_prev, V, alpha, sim_p, 'credited')
        rows.append(row); receipts.append(rc)
        _check(led, st, V, diag)

    t_sell = N + 1
    V_prev = V
    V_sell = V * (1.0 + g_sell)
    led.post(t_sell, 'growth', 'market', 'family_equity', st['f'] * (V_sell - V_prev))
    led.post(t_sell, 'growth', 'market', 'state_equity',  st['s'] * (V_sell - V_prev))
    W_sell = st['f'] * V_sell
    L_sell, rate_sell, delta_sell = _assess(W_sell, st['W'], st['cum'], sim_p)
    led.post(t_sell, 'sale', 'family_equity', 'family_cash', st['f'] * V_sell, units=st['f'])
    led.post(t_sell, 'tax_sell', 'family_cash', 'state_cash', L_sell, credited=L_sell)
    receipts.append((t_sell, 'tax_sell', L_sell, L_sell))
    cum = st['cum'] + L_sell
    f_after_sale = st['f']
    st['f'] = 0.0
    _check(led, st, V_sell, diag, units_held=False)
    tw_naive = led.bal['family_cash']

    cash, basis, i = tw_naive, tw_naive, 0      # post-sale basis = post-sale cash (BASIS_CHANGE)
    while i < SETTLE_MAX_ITER:
        L, _, delta = _assess(cash, basis, cum, sim_p)
        if abs(delta) < SETTLE_TOL and abs(cum) < SETTLE_TOL:
            break
        if abs(L) < SETTLE_TOL:
            break
        t_i = t_sell + i + 1
        led.post(t_i, 'tax_settle', 'family_cash', 'state_cash', L, credited=L)
        receipts.append((t_i, 'tax_settle', L, L))
        cash -= L
        basis = cash
        cum  += L
        i    += 1
    _check(led, st, V_sell, diag, units_held=False)

    if abs(cash - led.bal['family_cash']) > 1e-9 * V_sell:
        raise AssertionError('run_life: settlement cash disagrees with ledger')

    def _sum(kind):
        return sum(v for (_, k, v, _) in receipts if k == kind)

    return {
        'alpha': alpha, 'N': N,
        'TW_settled':  led.bal['family_cash'],
        'TW_naive':    tw_naive,
        'Net_settled': sum(c for (_, _, _, c) in receipts),
        'envelope_end': cum,
        'f_N': f_after_sale, 'W_sell': W_sell, 'V_sell': V_sell,
        'hold_true':   _sum('tax_inkind'),
        'sell_L':      _sum('tax_sell'),
        'settle_net':  _sum('tax_settle'),
        'settle_iters': i,
        'rows': rows, 'receipts': receipts, 'ledger': led, 'diag': diag,
    }


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P2 / P2b — FAMILY OVER HORIZON T, DEATH EVERY G YEARS, HEIR
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _heir_arrival(led, t, st, V, alpha, sim_p, envelope_unit, rule,
                  idx=1.0, refund_rule='legacy'):
    """
    Death at date t, after the decedent's own year-t assessment (plan D4: for
    Route C the delta from last assessment to death is zero). The heir receives
    the stake after tax with a clean envelope (D10): cum, cum_true and u_out
    are reset, so the heir can be refunded only units the heir has paid.

      'delta'         (D6)  prior net worth 0 (H = 0), influx = declared value of
                            the stake received, taxed in kind at tau(W_heir).
      'fresh_entrant' (CLOSE 4.1) no tax; basis = declared value of the stake.
    Returns the receipt tuple or None.
    """
    W_new = st['f'] * alpha * V
    st['cum'] = 0.0
    st['cum_true'] = 0.0
    st['u_out'] = 0.0
    if rule == 'fresh_entrant':
        st['W'] = W_new
        return None
    q, L, _, _ = _assess_c(st, W_new, 0.0, alpha, sim_p, idx, envelope_unit, refund_rule)
    _, paid = _pay_in_kind(led, t, 'tax_heir', st, V, L, q)
    st['W'] = st['f'] * alpha * V                # POST-heir-tax basis (BASIS_CHANGE)
    return (t, 'tax_heir', paid, L)


def run_family(p: dict, alpha: float, g_series: list, G: int | None,
               heir_influx: str, envelope_unit: str,
               consumption: float = 0.0, index_rate: float = 0.0,
               refund_rule: str = 'legacy') -> dict:
    """
    Route C family over T = len(g_series) years. Deaths at t = G, 2G, ... < T
    (G = None or G >= T: a single life). No sale and no verification event, so
    nothing ever reveals the true value: lambda = 0 (plan D9).

    consumption : share of net worth consumed each year (D16); 0 = none.
    index_rate  : W_min / k index growth per year (D16); 0 = unindexed.
    refund_rule : 'legacy' | 'ratio_mirror' (see module docstring).
    """
    if heir_influx not in _HEIR_RULES:
        raise ValueError(f'heir_influx must be one of {_HEIR_RULES}, got {heir_influx!r}')
    if envelope_unit not in _ENVELOPE_UNITS:
        raise ValueError(f'envelope_unit must be one of {_ENVELOPE_UNITS}, got {envelope_unit!r}')
    if refund_rule not in _REFUND_RULES:
        raise ValueError(f'refund_rule must be one of {_REFUND_RULES}, got {refund_rule!r}')
    sim_p = rate_params(p)
    T     = len(g_series)
    V     = p['V0_m']
    st    = _new_state(alpha, V)
    led   = Ledger()
    receipts: list[tuple] = []
    diag  = _new_diag()
    rows  = []
    gen   = 0
    deaths = []

    led.post(0, 'endow', 'market', 'family_equity', V)
    _check(led, st, V, diag)
    rows.append({'t': 0, 'gen': 0, 'event': 'entry', 'V': V, 'W': st['W'], 'f': 1.0,
                 's': 0.0, 'cum': 0.0, 'L': 0.0})

    for t in range(1, T + 1):
        V_prev = V
        V      = V * (1.0 + g_series[t - 1])
        idx    = (1.0 + index_rate) ** t
        row, rc = _holding_year(led, t, st, V_prev, V, alpha, sim_p, envelope_unit,
                                idx, refund_rule, consumption)
        row.update({'gen': gen, 'event': 'year'})
        rows.append(row); receipts.append(rc)
        _check(led, st, V, diag)
        if G is not None and t % G == 0 and t < T:
            gen += 1
            rc = _heir_arrival(led, t, st, V, alpha, sim_p, envelope_unit, heir_influx,
                               idx, refund_rule)
            if rc is not None:
                receipts.append(rc)
            deaths.append(t)
            rows.append({'t': t, 'gen': gen, 'event': 'heir', 'V': V, 'W': st['W'],
                         'f': st['f'], 's': st['s'], 'cum': st['cum'],
                         'L': rc[3] if rc else 0.0})
            _check(led, st, V, diag)

    return {
        'alpha': alpha, 'T': T, 'G': G, 'heir_influx': heir_influx,
        'envelope_unit': envelope_unit, 'consumption': consumption,
        'index_rate': index_rate, 'refund_rule': refund_rule, 'deaths': deaths,
        'f_T': st['f'], 's_T': st['s'], 'V_T': V, 'u_out_T': st['u_out'],
        'family_true_T': st['f'] * V, 'state_stake_true_T': st['s'] * V,
        'consumed_true': led.bal['consumed'],
        'net_credited': sum(c for (_, _, _, c) in receipts),
        'rows': rows, 'receipts': receipts, 'ledger': led, 'diag': diag,
    }


def family_pair(p: dict, alpha: float, g_series: list, G: int | None,
                heir_influx: str, envelope_unit: str, rho: float,
                honest: dict | None = None, **opts) -> dict:
    """
    Compare `alpha` with the honest family on the same path and rules.
    `opts` are the P2b switches (consumption, index_rate, refund_rule), applied
    to both families.

      gain            f_T(a)/f_T(1) - 1         + = family ends with more (BRG)
      state_stake_rel s_T(a)/s_T(1) - 1         state's terminal stake vs honest
      pv_rel          (PV(a)-PV(1))/PV(1)       PV of true value received, at rho;
                                                None where PV(1) < pv_rel_min_frac x
                                                honest terminal family value
      consumed_rel    consumed(a)/consumed(1)-1 diagnostic only (D11 objective is
                                                terminal net worth)
    """
    h = honest if honest is not None else run_family(p, 1.0, g_series, G, heir_influx,
                                                     envelope_unit, **opts)
    a = h if alpha == 1.0 else run_family(p, alpha, g_series, G, heir_influx,
                                          envelope_unit, **opts)
    pv_h, pv_a = pv_true(h, rho), pv_true(a, rho)
    return {
        'gain':            a['f_T'] / h['f_T'] - 1.0,
        'state_stake_rel': (a['s_T'] / h['s_T'] - 1.0) if h['s_T'] > 1e-12 else None,
        'pv_rel':          ((pv_a - pv_h) / pv_h
                            if pv_h >= p['val_gen']['pv_rel_min_frac'] * abs(h['family_true_T']) else None),
        'consumed_rel':    ((a['consumed_true'] / h['consumed_true'] - 1.0)
                            if h['consumed_true'] > 1e-12 else None),
        'f_T': a['f_T'], 'f_T_honest': h['f_T'], 'V_T': h['V_T'],
        'T': a['T'], 'n_deaths': len(a['deaths']),
    }


def alignment(cells: dict, state_tol: float) -> dict:
    """
    Plan §6 alignment over a {alpha: family_pair result} dict, alpha != 1.
    conflict : family gains (gain > 0) and the state is outside +-state_tol
    aligned  : family gains and the state is within tolerance
    undefined: pv_rel is None (honest PV too small)
    """
    out = {'conflict': [], 'aligned': [], 'undefined': [], 'no_gain': []}
    for a, m in cells.items():
        if m.get('is_honest') or str(a) == '1.0':
            continue
        if m['gain'] <= 0.0:
            out['no_gain'].append(a)
        elif m['pv_rel'] is None:
            out['undefined'].append(a)
        elif abs(m['pv_rel']) > state_tol:
            out['conflict'].append(a)
        else:
            out['aligned'].append(a)
    return out


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P3 — FOUR ROUTES (A, B, C, D): a ledger wrapper over wdt_kernel
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The route mechanics (growth, consumption, declared price, verification, ONE assessment on total declared W,
# allocation by delta shares, settlement per route, death and heir) live in wdt_kernel (D12). This file owns
#   * the double-entry ledger, the receipts and the invariants (a Flows -> ledger-post translation, _LedgerHook);
#   * the strategy library and its batched search (a line axis in the kernel: one line per strategy);
#   * the verdict tests.
# One driver (_drive) runs both: run_family3 is the n = 1 case with the ledger attached; run_batch runs many
# strategies as lines with no ledger. They share every operation, so they cannot disagree (checked in
# _p3_validate and in main).
#
# Per-route declared price (full-asset basis): A, B true value; C alpha_C x true value, paid in kind at the
# declared price; D alpha_D x true value between voluntary resets, the true price at a reset, at a death
# auction, and for the share vD already auctioned (hazard lambda_D).
#
# RETIRED (WDT_Refactor_Plan D6): the scheduled Route D `reset_interval` and the `death_waiver`. A reset is an ACTION
# the family chooses (`reset=`: every m years, an explicit set of years, or a function of ctx), so it is part of a
# strategy, not of the rule set. Death always holds the Route D auction. lambda_C (Route C verification) and
# lambda_D (Route D corrective auction) are independent inputs.

_ROUTES = ('A', 'B', 'C', 'D')
_IN_KIND = ('C', 'Cv')       # routes paid in kind, each with its own units-paid cap
_C_CAP = wk.C_CAPS
_B_MODES = wk.B_MODES
_SETTLE_KINDS = ('reset_D', 'death_D', 'death_B', 'terminal_D', 'terminal_B')   # receipts carry the bare kind


def _alpha_at(spec, ctx):
    """A declaration ratio is a number, or a function of ctx (t, gen, yrs_in_gen, yrs_to_death, yrs_to_reset)."""
    return spec(ctx) if callable(spec) else spec


def _ctx(t, gen, gen_start, G, T, cycle=0):
    """Strategy context. `cycle` is the STRATEGY's own voluntary reset interval (0 = none); it only feeds yrs_to_reset."""
    tt = max(t, 1)
    if G:
        nd = -(-tt // G) * G
        to_death = (nd - t) if nd < T else (T - t)
    else:
        to_death = T - t
    to_reset = (-(-tt // cycle) * cycle - t) if cycle > 0 else 10 ** 6
    return {'t': t, 'gen': gen, 'yrs_in_gen': t - gen_start,
            'yrs_to_death': to_death, 'yrs_to_reset': to_reset}


def _rate_fn(p: dict):
    """The kernel's rate_fn: wdt_core.rate_vec bound to the rate parameters of p (the schedule lives in wdt_core)."""
    rp = rate_params(p)
    q = {'k': rp['k'], 'tau_0': rp['tau_0'], 'tau_m': rp['tau_m'], 'wmin': rp['W_min']}
    if 'schedule' in rp:
        q['schedule'] = rp['schedule']
        if 'ladder' in rp:
            q['ladder'] = rp['ladder']
    return lambda x: rate_vec(x, q)


def _p3_routes(shares: dict) -> list:
    routes = [r for r in _ROUTES if shares.get(r, 0.0) > 0.0]
    tot = sum(shares[r] for r in routes)
    if not routes or abs(tot - 1.0) > 1e-9:
        raise ValueError(f'route shares must be positive and sum to 1, got {shares!r}')
    return routes


def _at(x, i=0):
    """Element i of a Flows entry (array of length n, or a scalar 0.0)."""
    a = np.asarray(x, dtype=float).reshape(-1)
    return float(a[i if a.size > 1 else 0])


def _reset_years(spec, T: int, G) -> tuple:
    """Years of a voluntary Route D reset. spec: None | int m (every m years) | iterable of years | f(ctx) -> bool."""
    if spec is None or spec == 0:
        return ()
    if callable(spec):
        return tuple(t for t in range(1, T + 1) if spec(_ctx(t, 0, 0, G, T, 0)))
    if isinstance(spec, int):
        return tuple(range(spec, T + 1, spec))
    return tuple(sorted({int(t) for t in spec if 1 <= int(t) <= T}))


def _cycle_of(spec) -> int:
    return spec if isinstance(spec, int) and not isinstance(spec, bool) else 0


def _p3_new_diag():
    return {'cons_err': 0.0, 'unit_err': 0.0, 'min_E_cash': 0.0, 'min_A_D': 0.0,
            'min_u_out': 0.0, 'min_state_units': 0.0, 'uout_err': 0.0, 'min_EC': 0.0}


def _book_diag(book, diag):
    """Fold the kernel's own invariants (min E_cash, A_D, EC, units) into diag."""
    c = book.check()
    diag['cons_err'] = max(diag['cons_err'], c['units'])
    diag['min_E_cash'] = min(diag['min_E_cash'], c['min_E_cash'])
    diag['min_A_D'] = min(diag['min_A_D'], c['min_A_D'])
    diag['min_EC'] = min(diag['min_EC'], c['min_EC'])
    diag['min_state_units'] = min(diag['min_state_units'], c['min_state_units'])
    diag['min_u_out'] = min(diag['min_u_out'], c['min_uo'])
    diag['uout_err'] = max(diag['uout_err'], c['uo_excess'])


# ── the one driver (_run_kernel) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

def _run_kernel(p: dict, lines: list, g_series: list, G, heir_influx: str, o: dict, reset_years: tuple, hook=None):
    """
    Run the kernel over len(g_series) years for `lines` (dicts with 'aC', 'aD', 'shares', 'cycle'); every line shares
    the reset years and the Route B mode in `o`. `hook(t, kind, flows, book, gen)` sees every operation; pseudo-kinds
    'endow' (t = 0), 'year_end' and 'death_end' mark the points where invariants and rows are taken.
    """
    n, T = len(lines), len(g_series)
    rate_fn = _rate_fn(p)
    V0 = {r: np.array([ln['shares'].get(r, 0.0) * p['V0_m'] for ln in lines]) for r in _ROUTES}
    has_cv = (o['verify_hazard'] > 0.0 or o['death_verify']) and bool(np.any(V0['C'] > 0.0))
    c0 = [_ctx(0, 0, 0, G, T, ln['cycle']) for ln in lines]
    a0 = {'C': np.array([_alpha_at(ln['aC'], c) for ln, c in zip(lines, c0)], dtype=float),
          'D': np.array([_alpha_at(ln['aD'], c) for ln, c in zip(lines, c0)], dtype=float)}
    book = wk.Book(n, V0, alpha0=a0, has_cv=has_cv, b_mode=o['route_b'], c_cap=o['c_cap'],
                   verify_down=o['verify_down'], r_def=o['r_def'],
                   inc_allow=o['income_cap'] * o['income_ratio'] * p['V0_m'])
    rset = set(reset_years)
    gen, gen_start = 0, 0
    if hook:
        hook(0, 'endow', None, book, gen)
    for t in range(1, T + 1):
        idx = (1.0 + o['index_rate']) ** t
        ctxs = [_ctx(t, gen, gen_start, G, T, ln['cycle']) for ln in lines]
        aC = np.array([_alpha_at(ln['aC'], c) for ln, c in zip(lines, ctxs)], dtype=float)
        aD = np.array([_alpha_at(ln['aD'], c) for ln, c in zip(lines, ctxs)], dtype=float)
        ops = wk.step_year(book, rate_fn, idx, g_series[t - 1], o['consumption'], aC, aD,
                           o['verify_hazard'], o['verify_hazard_D'], t in rset)
        if hook:
            for kind, fl in ops:
                hook(t, kind, fl, book, gen)
            hook(t, 'year_end', None, book, gen)
        if G is not None and t % G == 0 and t < T:
            gen += 1
            gen_start = t
            ops = wk.step_death(book, rate_fn, idx, heir_influx, o['death_verify'])
            if hook:
                for kind, fl in ops:
                    hook(t, kind, fl, book, gen)
                hook(t, 'death_end', None, book, gen)
    ops = wk.settle_terminal(book)
    if hook:
        for kind, fl in ops:
            hook(T, kind, fl, book, gen)
        hook(T, 'terminal_end', None, book, gen)
    return book


# ── ledger hook (n = 1) ────────────────────────────────────────

class _LedgerHook:
    """Translates the kernel's Flows into ledger posts, receipts, rows and invariant checks (one line)."""

    def __init__(self, routes, T):
        self.led = Ledger(tuple(['market', 'consumed'] + [f'family_{r}' for r in routes]
                                + [f'state_{r}' for r in routes] + ['income', 'state_cash']))
        self.receipts, self.rows, self.deaths = [], [], []
        self.diag = _p3_new_diag()
        self.verified = []
        self._last_tax = None

    def _post_value(self, t, kind, fl, rk=None):
        for r, v in fl.value.items():
            v = _at(v)
            cr = _at(fl.credited.get(r, 0.0))
            if v != 0.0:
                self.led.post(t, kind, f'family_{r}', f'state_{r}', v, route=r, units=_at(fl.units.get(r, 0.0)))
            if v != 0.0 or cr != 0.0:
                self.receipts.append((t, kind if kind in _SETTLE_KINDS else f'{kind}_{r}', v, cr))
        inc = _at(fl.income)
        if inc != 0.0:
            self.led.post(t, f'{kind}_income', 'income', 'state_cash', inc, route='B')
            self.receipts.append((t, f'{kind}_B_income', inc, inc))

    def _invariants(self, book):
        d, led = self.diag, self.led
        for r, x in book.R.items():
            V = float(x['V'][0])
            if V > 0.0:
                d['unit_err'] = max(d['unit_err'],
                                    abs(led.bal[f'family_{r}'] - float(x['f'][0]) * V) / V,
                                    abs(led.bal[f'state_{r}'] - float(x['s'][0]) * V) / V)
        _book_diag(book, d)

    def __call__(self, t, kind, fl, book, gen):
        led = self.led
        if kind == 'endow':
            for r in book.routes:
                if r != 'Cv':
                    led.post(0, 'endow', 'market', f'family_{r}', float(book.R[r]['V'][0]))
            self._invariants(book)
        elif kind == 'growth':
            for r in book.routes:
                led.post(t, 'growth', 'market', f'family_{r}', _at(fl.growth_family[r]))
                led.post(t, 'growth', 'market', f'state_{r}', _at(fl.growth_state[r]))
                cv = _at(fl.consumed[r])
                if cv != 0.0:
                    cu = cv / float(book.R[r]['V'][0])
                    led.post(t, 'consume', f'family_{r}', 'consumed', cv, units=cu)
        elif kind in ('verify', 'verify_death'):
            V = float(book.R['C']['V'][0])
            mf, ms = _at(fl.verify_family), _at(fl.verify_state)
            if mf > 0.0:
                led.post(t, 'verify', 'family_C', 'family_Cv', mf * V, units=mf)
            if ms > 0.0:
                led.post(t, 'verify', 'state_C', 'state_Cv', ms * V, units=ms)
        elif kind in ('tax', 'tax_death_C', 'tax_death', 'tax_heir', 'reset_D') or kind in _SETTLE_KINDS:
            self._post_value(t, kind, fl)
            if kind == 'tax':
                self._last_tax = fl
        elif kind == 'year_end':
            fl = self._last_tax
            sh = float(wk.verified_share(book)[0])
            self.verified.append(sh)
            self.rows.append({'t': t, 'gen': gen, 'W': float(sum(book.declared().values())[0]),
                              'delta': _at(fl.delta), 'L': _at(fl.L), 'rate': _at(fl.rate),
                              'A_D': float(book.A_D[0]), 'E_cash': float(book.E_cash[0]),
                              'u_out': {r: float(v[0]) for r, v in book.uo.items()}, 'verified_share': sh})
            self._invariants(book)
        elif kind == 'death_end':
            self.deaths.append(t)
            self.rows.append({'t': t, 'gen': gen, 'event': 'heir', 'A_D': float(book.A_D[0])})
            self._invariants(book)
        elif kind == 'terminal_end':
            self._invariants(book)


def _norm_opts(p: dict, opts: dict) -> dict:
    """Defaults and validation of the run switches (shared by run_family3 and run_batch)."""
    o = {'consumption': 0.0, 'index_rate': 0.0, 'shares': None, 'verify_hazard': 0.0, 'c_cap': 'units',
         'verify_down': 'allow', 'verify_hazard_D': 0.0, 'route_b': 'sale', 'r_def': 0.0, 'income_ratio': 0.0,
         'income_cap': 1.0, 'death_verify': False, 'reset': None}
    unknown = set(opts) - set(o)
    if unknown:
        raise TypeError(f'unknown run switch(es) {sorted(unknown)}; the scheduled reset_interval and death_waiver are retired (use reset=)')
    o.update(opts)
    if o['verify_down'] not in ('allow', 'reset'):
        raise ValueError(f"verify_down must be 'allow' or 'reset', got {o['verify_down']!r}")
    if not 0.0 <= o['verify_hazard_D'] <= 1.0:
        raise ValueError(f"verify_hazard_D must be in [0, 1], got {o['verify_hazard_D']!r}")
    if o['c_cap'] not in _C_CAP:
        raise ValueError(f"c_cap must be one of {_C_CAP}, got {o['c_cap']!r}")
    if not 0.0 <= o['verify_hazard'] <= 1.0:
        raise ValueError(f"verify_hazard must be in [0, 1], got {o['verify_hazard']!r}")
    if o['route_b'] not in _B_MODES:
        raise ValueError(f"route_b must be one of {_B_MODES}, got {o['route_b']!r}")
    if not 0.0 <= o['income_cap'] <= 1.0:
        raise ValueError(f"income_cap must be in [0, 1], got {o['income_cap']!r}")
    if o['income_ratio'] < 0.0:
        raise ValueError(f"income_ratio must be >= 0, got {o['income_ratio']!r}")
    if o['r_def'] <= -1.0:
        raise ValueError(f"r_def must be > -1, got {o['r_def']!r}")
    o['shares'] = dict(o['shares'] if o['shares'] is not None else p['val_gen']['route_shares'])
    return o


def run_family3(p: dict, alpha_C, alpha_D, g_series: list, G: int | None, heir_influx: str, **opts) -> dict:
    """
    Four-route family over T = len(g_series) years; deaths at G, 2G, ... < T. A ledger wrapper over wdt_kernel (n = 1).
    Refunds follow the ratio-mirror rule (D8); a Route D write-down cancels accrued liability first, then refunds in
    units like A/B (symmetric).

    alpha_C, alpha_D  numbers, or functions of ctx (see _ctx): a declaration strategy.
    reset           the family's voluntary Route D hard reset (an ACTION, D6): None | m (every m years) | iterable of
                    years | f(ctx) -> bool. At a reset the declared price is the true price and the accrued liability
                    is settled in units at the true price. Death always holds the Route D auction (no waiver).
    consumption, index_rate, shares   as before (D16, route shares of V0).
    verify_hazard   lambda_C: per-year probability that an unverified Route C asset is verified (D9); the share moves to a
                    verified tranche Cv declared at the true value. 0 = none.
    verify_hazard_D lambda_D: the same expected-value corrective auction on Route D (VAL 11.3), independent of lambda_C: a
                    share vD = 1 - (1 - lambda_D)^t is declared at the true price, the rest follows the strategy.
    c_cap           'units' | 'units_and_value' (Route C refund cap, plan check 6, E2).
    verify_down     'allow' | 'reset' (correcting your own overstatement: write-down | basis reset with no refund).
    route_b         Route B payment mode (D4b/D4c): 'sale' | 'lien' (balance accrues at r_def, settled at death and the
                    horizon) | 'income' (external income income_cap x income_ratio x V0_m x index, shortfall sold).
    death_verify    death verifies Route C with certainty (D6).
    Family terminal net worth = sum of true route holdings at T after settling outstanding Route D liability at the
    true price and any deferred Route B balance.
    """
    if heir_influx not in _HEIR_RULES:
        raise ValueError(f'heir_influx must be one of {_HEIR_RULES}, got {heir_influx!r}')
    o = _norm_opts(p, opts)
    shares = o['shares']
    routes = _p3_routes(shares)
    T = len(g_series)
    rys = _reset_years(o['reset'], T, G)
    ln = {'aC': alpha_C, 'aD': alpha_D, 'shares': shares, 'cycle': _cycle_of(o['reset'])}
    all_routes = routes + (['Cv'] if ((o['verify_hazard'] > 0.0 or o['death_verify']) and 'C' in routes) else [])
    hook = _LedgerHook(all_routes, T)
    book = _run_kernel(p, [ln], g_series, G, heir_influx, o, rys, hook)
    led = hook.led
    if abs(sum(led.bal.values())) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, float(book.family_true()[0])):
        raise AssertionError('run_family3: ledger does not balance')
    R = book.R
    return {
        'alpha_C': alpha_C, 'alpha_D': alpha_D, 'T': T, 'G': G, 'routes': all_routes,
        'deaths': hook.deaths, 'shares': dict(shares), 'consumption': o['consumption'],
        'index_rate': o['index_rate'], 'reset_years': list(rys), 'verify_hazard': o['verify_hazard'],
        'verify_hazard_D': o['verify_hazard_D'], 'c_cap': o['c_cap'],
        'verified_share': hook.verified,
        'family_true_T': float(book.family_true()[0]),
        'state_true_T': float(book.state_true()[0]),
        'consumed_true': led.bal['consumed'],
        'f_T': {r: float(x['f'][0]) for r, x in R.items()},
        'lost_refund': float(book.lost_refund[0]), 'unpaid_D': float(book.unpaid_D[0]),
        'route_b': o['route_b'], 'unpaid_B': float(book.unpaid_B[0]), 'income_paid': float(book.inc_total[0]),
        'receipts': hook.receipts, 'rows': hook.rows, 'ledger': led, 'diag': hook.diag,
    }


# ── the batched engine (strategy search) ───────────────────────

class _PvHook:
    """Accumulates the PV of the state's receipts (true value) per line and discount rate; folds invariants."""

    def __init__(self, n, rhos):
        self.rhos = list(rhos)
        self.pv = {r: np.zeros(n) for r in self.rhos}
        self.n = n
        self.diag = _p3_new_diag()

    def __call__(self, t, kind, fl, book, gen):
        if fl is not None and (fl.value or np.any(fl.income != 0.0)):
            tot = sum((np.broadcast_to(np.asarray(v, dtype=float), (self.n,)) for v in fl.value.values()), np.zeros(self.n))
            tot = tot + fl.income
            for r in self.rhos:
                self.pv[r] += tot / (1.0 + r) ** t
        if kind in ('year_end', 'death_end', 'terminal_end'):
            _book_diag(book, self.diag)


def run_batch(p: dict, lines: list, g_series: list, G, heir_influx: str, rhos=(), **opts) -> dict:
    """
    Run many strategies at once, one kernel line each. `lines` are dicts {'aC', 'aD'} (numbers or functions of ctx) with
    optional per-line overrides 'shares', 'reset', 'route_b' (a strategy's own route migration, reset action and Route B
    election). Lines are grouped by (reset years, Route B mode) because those are scalar in the kernel.
    Returns arrays in the order of `lines`: family_true_T, state_true_T, lost_refund, unpaid_D, pv[rho], and a worst-case diag.
    """
    if heir_influx not in _HEIR_RULES:
        raise ValueError(f'heir_influx must be one of {_HEIR_RULES}, got {heir_influx!r}')
    base = _norm_opts(p, opts)
    T = len(g_series)
    groups = {}
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines):
        o = dict(base)
        for k in ('shares', 'reset', 'route_b'):
            if ln.get(k) is not None:
                o[k] = ln[k]
        o = _norm_opts(p, o)
        rys = _reset_years(o['reset'], T, G)
        key = (rys, o['route_b'])
        groups.setdefault(key, []).append((i, dict(aC=ln['aC'], aD=ln['aD'], shares=o['shares'], cycle=_cycle_of(o['reset'])), o))
    n = len(lines)
    out = {'family_true_T': np.zeros(n), 'state_true_T': np.zeros(n), 'lost_refund': np.zeros(n), 'unpaid_D': np.zeros(n),
           'pv': {r: np.zeros(n) for r in rhos}, 'diag': _p3_new_diag()}
    for (rys, _mode), members in groups.items():
        idxs = [m[0] for m in members]
        o = members[0][2]
        hook = _PvHook(len(members), rhos)
        book = _run_kernel(p, [m[1] for m in members], g_series, G, heir_influx, o, rys, hook)
        out['family_true_T'][idxs] = book.family_true()
        out['state_true_T'][idxs] = book.state_true()
        out['lost_refund'][idxs] = book.lost_refund
        out['unpaid_D'][idxs] = book.unpaid_D
        for r in rhos:
            out['pv'][r][idxs] = hook.pv[r]
        d = out['diag']
        for k in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            d[k] = max(d[k], hook.diag[k])
        for k in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units', 'min_EC'):
            d[k] = min(d[k], hook.diag[k])
    return out


def _batch_metrics(p: dict, B: dict, i: int, h: int = 0) -> dict:
    """family3_pair-style metrics of line i against the honest line h of a run_batch result."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    f_h, f_a = B['family_true_T'][h], B['family_true_T'][i]
    s_h, s_a = B['state_true_T'][h], B['state_true_T'][i]

    def pv_rel(rho):
        ph, pa = B['pv'][rho][h], B['pv'][rho][i]
        return (pa - ph) / ph if ph >= vg['pv_rel_min_frac'] * abs(f_h) else None
    return {'gain': float(f_a / f_h - 1.0),
            'state_rel': float(s_a / s_h - 1.0) if s_h > 1e-12 else None,
            'pv_rel': pv_rel(p['rho']),
            'pv_rel_by_rho': {str(r_): pv_rel(r_) for r_ in (p.get('rho_sens') or [])},
            'TW': float(f_a), 'TW_honest': float(f_h), 'lost_refund': float(B['lost_refund'][i])}


def _rhos(p: dict) -> list:
    return sorted({p['rho']} | set(p.get('rho_sens') or []))


def _pv_rel_at(p: dict, h: dict, a: dict, rho: float):
    """(PV(a) - PV(h)) / PV(h) of the state's receipts at discount rate rho; None where the honest PV is too small (as family3_pair)."""
    pv_h, pv_a = pv_true(h, rho), pv_true(a, rho)
    return ((pv_a - pv_h) / pv_h if pv_h >= p['val_gen']['pv_rel_min_frac'] * abs(h['family_true_T']) else None)


def family3_pair(p: dict, alpha_C, alpha_D, g_series: list, G: int | None,
                 heir_influx: str, rho: float, honest: dict | None = None, own: dict | None = None, **opts) -> dict:
    """
    Compare (alpha_C, alpha_D) with the honest family (1, 1) on the same rules.
      gain          TW(a)/TW(1) - 1   TW = family true net worth at T (BRG)
      state_rel     state true holdings at T, vs honest
      pv_rel        (PV(a) - PV(1)) / PV(1), PV of true value received (SPT)
    `own` holds switches that belong to the STRATEGY and not to the rule set (reset=, shares=, route_b=): they apply to
    the strategy run only, the honest family keeps `opts`.
    """
    h = honest if honest is not None else run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, g_series, G, heir_influx, **opts)
    is_h = (not callable(alpha_C) and not callable(alpha_D)
            and alpha_C == 1.0 and alpha_D == 1.0 and not own)
    a = h if is_h else run_family3(p, alpha_C, alpha_D, g_series, G, heir_influx, **{**opts, **(own or {})})
    pv_h, pv_a = pv_true(h, rho), pv_true(a, rho)
    return {
        'is_honest': is_h,
        'gain':      a['family_true_T'] / h['family_true_T'] - 1.0,
        'state_rel': (a['state_true_T'] / h['state_true_T'] - 1.0) if h['state_true_T'] > 1e-12 else None,
        'pv_rel':    ((pv_a - pv_h) / pv_h
                      if pv_h >= p['val_gen']['pv_rel_min_frac'] * abs(h['family_true_T']) else None),
        'consumed_rel': ((a['consumed_true'] / h['consumed_true'] - 1.0)
                         if h['consumed_true'] > 1e-12 else None),
        'pv_rel_by_rho': {str(r_): _pv_rel_at(p, h, a, r_) for r_ in (p.get('rho_sens') or [])},   # SPT sensitivity (D1c)
        'TW': a['family_true_T'], 'TW_honest': h['family_true_T'],
        'lost_refund': a['lost_refund'], 'unpaid_D': a['unpaid_D'],
    }


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# METRICS FROM THE LEDGER
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def pv_true(run: dict, rho: float) -> float:
    """PV at t=0 of every receipt by the state, valued at true value surrendered."""
    return sum(v / (1.0 + rho) ** t for (t, _, v, _) in run['receipts'])


def pair(p: dict, alpha: float, g_series: list, g_sell: float, rho: float,
         honest: dict | None = None) -> dict:
    """Compare `alpha` with the honest declarer (P1 frame). Legacy metrics plus pv_rel."""
    h = honest if honest is not None else run_life(p, 1.0, g_series, g_sell)
    a = h if alpha == 1.0 else run_life(p, alpha, g_series, g_sell)
    d = h['TW_settled'] if abs(h['TW_settled']) > 1e-12 else 1.0
    pv_h, pv_a = pv_true(h, rho), pv_true(a, rho)
    tw_gap = (a['TW_settled'] - h['TW_settled']) / d
    return {
        'net_pct': (a['Net_settled'] - h['Net_settled']) / d,
        'tw_gap':  tw_gap,
        'tw_cost': -tw_gap,
        'pv_pct':  (pv_a - pv_h) / d,
        'pv_rel':  ((pv_a - pv_h) / pv_h) if pv_h >= p['val_gen']['pv_rel_min_frac'] * abs(d) else None,
        'pv_honest': pv_h,
        'N': h['N'],
    }


def _decomp(run: dict) -> dict:
    """Plan §1 decomposition of one run, £m."""
    return {
        'alpha': run['alpha'], 'N': run['N'],
        'holding_payments_true': run['hold_true'],
        'sell_year_cash':        run['sell_L'],
        'post_sale_settlement':  run['settle_net'],
        'TW_before_settlement':  run['TW_naive'],
        'TW_settled':            run['TW_settled'],
        'net_credited':          run['Net_settled'],
        'settle_iters':          run['settle_iters'],
    }


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRIDGE TO LEGACY AND VALIDATION (P1)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _bridge_series(p: dict, need: int) -> tuple:
    """
    The series of the bridge's 'historical' leg: the REAL capital-return series of the JST country [rates].uk_iso
    (wdt_jst.real_return_series, the same data VAL replays and RATES reads), its longest run of consecutive calendar years.
    Replaces the nominal canonical series p['returns'] (retired with the scenario start year, D11). Needs `need` values.
    Returns (series, info).
    """
    rp = p['rates']
    r = real_return_series(load_jst(rp['jst_path']), rp['uk_iso'])
    years = sorted(r)
    best, cur = [], []
    for y in years:
        cur = cur + [y] if cur and y == cur[-1] + 1 else [y]
        if len(cur) > len(best):
            best = list(cur)
    if len(best) < need:
        raise ValueError(f"bridge: the longest consecutive run of {rp['uk_iso']} real returns is {len(best)} years, need {need}")
    return [r[y] for y in best], {'source': 'jst_real_capital_return', 'iso': rp['uk_iso'], 'first': best[0],
                                  'last': best[-1], 'n': len(best), 'jst_path': rp['jst_path']}


def _bridge(p: dict) -> dict:
    """
    Plan §7 check 2. Compare run_life / pair with legacy run_pair (constant g)
    and run_sim_hist (a real JST return series, D1a) over the grids the legacy VAL tables use.
    """
    sw   = p['sweep']
    N    = p['N_val']
    rho  = p['rho']
    alphas = sw['alpha_vals']
    gs     = sw['g_vals']
    ns     = sw['n_actual_vals']
    g0     = p['g_real']

    worst = {'net_pct': 0.0, 'tw_gap': 0.0, 'pv_pct': 0.0,
             'hist_TW': 0.0, 'hist_Net': 0.0}
    diag  = _new_diag()
    n_cells = 0

    def _absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            diag[key] = max(diag[key], d[key])
        diag['min_state_units'] = min(diag['min_state_units'], d['min_state_units'])
        diag['min_state_cash']  = min(diag['min_state_cash'],  d['min_state_cash'])

    def _const_cells():
        for g in gs:
            yield g, N
        for n in ns:
            yield g0, n

    seen = set()
    for g, n in _const_cells():
        if (g, n) in seen:
            continue
        seen.add((g, n))
        series = [g] * n
        h = run_life(p, 1.0, series, g)
        _absorb(h)
        for alpha in alphas:
            m   = pair(p, alpha, series, g, rho, honest=h)
            leg = run_pair(p, alpha, g, n)
            worst['net_pct'] = max(worst['net_pct'], abs(m['net_pct'] - leg['net_pct']))
            worst['tw_gap']  = max(worst['tw_gap'],  abs(m['tw_gap']  - leg['tw_gap']))
            worst['pv_pct']  = max(worst['pv_pct'],  abs(m['pv_pct']  - leg['pv_pct']))
            if alpha != 1.0:
                _absorb(run_life(p, alpha, series, g))
            n_cells += 1

    n_traj = sorted({5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, N})
    n_hist = 0
    jst_series, jst_info = _bridge_series(p, max(n_traj) + 1)
    p_hist = dict(p, returns=jst_series)               # run_sim_hist reads p['returns']; here a JST real series
    for n in n_traj:
        series, g_sell = jst_series[:n], jst_series[n]
        for alpha in alphas:
            r   = run_life(p, alpha, series, g_sell)
            leg = run_sim_hist(p_hist, alpha=alpha, N=n)
            worst['hist_TW']  = max(worst['hist_TW'],  abs(r['TW_settled']  - leg['TW_settled']))
            worst['hist_Net'] = max(worst['hist_Net'], abs(r['Net_settled'] - leg['Net_settled']))
            _absorb(r)
            n_hist += 1

    return {'max_abs_diff': worst, 'worst_diag': diag,
            'cells_constant_g': n_cells, 'cells_historical': n_hist,
            'historical_series': jst_info, 'tolerance': BRIDGE_TOL}


def _validate(p: dict, bridge: dict) -> dict:
    """Fail the run if any P1 check fails. Returns the report stored in meta."""
    report = {'N_val': p['N_val'], 'checks': {}, 'info': {}}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        report['checks'][name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    for key, v in bridge['max_abs_diff'].items():
        check(f'bridge_{key}', v < BRIDGE_TOL, f'max|diff|={v:.2e}')

    d = bridge['worst_diag']
    check('conservation_units_and_value', d['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL,
          f"max err={d['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('in_kind_identity_family_equity_eq_f_times_V', d['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL,
          f"max rel err={d['unit_err']:.2e}")

    series = [p['g_real']] * p['N_val']
    m = pair(p, 1.0, series, p['g_real'], p['rho'])
    check('honest_identity', max(abs(m['net_pct']), abs(m['tw_gap']), abs(m['pv_pct'])) < 1e-12)

    report['info']['min_state_units'] = d['min_state_units']
    report['info']['min_state_cash']  = d['min_state_cash']
    return report


def _flat(p: dict) -> dict:
    """Flat rate at tau_0 with no threshold (plan §1 flat-rate test)."""
    return dict(p, tau_m=p['tau_0'], W_min=0.0, schedule='logistic')


def _p2_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P2 checks (plan §7: 1, 3 for the no-sale frame, plus P2-specific ones)."""
    checks = {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    g      = p['g_real']
    vg     = p['val_gen']
    alphas = p['sweep']['alpha_vals']
    rho    = p['rho']
    diag   = _new_diag()

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            diag[key] = max(diag[key], d[key])
        diag['min_state_units'] = min(diag['min_state_units'], d['min_state_units'])

    sim_p = rate_params(p)
    worst = 0.0
    for a in alphas:
        for n in (30, 90):
            r   = run_family(p, a, [g] * n, None, 'delta', 'real')
            leg = simulate(p['V0_m'], [g] * n, a, sim_p)
            absorb(r)
            for row_new, row_old in zip([x for x in r['rows'] if x['event'] == 'year'], leg[1:]):
                for key in ('f', 'cum', 'L', 'W', 'V'):
                    worst = max(worst, abs(row_new[key] - row_old[key]))
    check('single_life_equals_legacy_simulate', worst < BRIDGE_TOL, f'max|diff|={worst:.2e}')

    bench = []
    worst = 0.0
    for (n, a), target in PLAN_S1_GAIN.items():
        h = run_family(p, 1.0, [g] * n, None, 'delta', 'real')
        r = run_family(p, a,   [g] * n, None, 'delta', 'real')
        gain = r['f_T'] / h['f_T'] - 1.0
        worst = max(worst, abs(gain - target))
        bench.append({'N': n, 'alpha': a, 'gain': gain, 'plan': target})
    applies = _plan_fixture_applies(p)
    if applies:
        check('plan_s1_no_verification_table', worst < PLAN_S1_TOL, f'max|diff| vs plan={worst:.4f}')
    else:
        checks['plan_s1_no_verification_table'] = {
            'ok': True, 'skipped': True,
            'detail': f'SKIPPED, parameters differ from the plan baseline (max|diff| would be {worst:.4f})'}

    fp = _flat(p)
    stakes = [run_family(fp, a, [g] * PLAN_S1_FLAT_N, None, 'delta', 'real')['f_T'] for a in alphas]
    spread = max(stakes) - min(stakes)
    check('flat_rate_stake_identical_across_alpha', spread < 1e-12, f'spread={spread:.2e}')
    if _plan_fixture_applies(p, ('tau_0', 'g_real')):     # the flat-rate stake depends on tau_0 and g only
        check('flat_rate_stake_equals_plan', abs(stakes[0] - PLAN_S1_FLAT_STAKE) < 5e-7,
              f'{stakes[0]:.6f} vs {PLAN_S1_FLAT_STAKE}')
    else:
        checks['flat_rate_stake_equals_plan'] = {
            'ok': True, 'skipped': True,
            'detail': f'SKIPPED, tau_0 or g differ from the plan baseline ({stakes[0]:.6f} vs {PLAN_S1_FLAT_STAKE})'}

    worst = 0.0
    for rule in _HEIR_RULES:
        for env in _ENVELOPE_UNITS:
            fs = []
            for a in alphas:
                r = run_family(fp, a, [g] * vg['T'], vg['G'], rule, env)
                absorb(r); fs.append(r['f_T'])
            worst = max(worst, max(fs) - min(fs))
    check('flat_rate_alpha_free_with_heirs', worst < 1e-12, f'spread={worst:.2e}')

    check('family_conservation_units_and_value', diag['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL,
          f"max err={diag['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('family_in_kind_identity', diag['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL,
          f"max rel err={diag['unit_err']:.2e}")

    series = [g] * vg['T']
    worst = 0.0
    for rule in _HEIR_RULES:
        for env in _ENVELOPE_UNITS:
            m = family_pair(p, 1.0, series, vg['G'], rule, env, rho)
            worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']), abs(m['state_stake_rel'] or 0.0), abs(m['pv_rel'] or 0.0))
    check('honest_identity_all_switches', worst < 1e-12)

    worst = 0.0
    for rule in _HEIR_RULES:
        for a in alphas:
            e1 = run_family(p, a, series, vg['G'], rule, 'credited')
            e2 = run_family(p, a, series, vg['G'], rule, 'real')
            worst = max(worst, abs(e1['f_T'] - e2['f_T']) / e1['f_T'])
    check('envelope_unit_inert_constant_alpha_no_sale', worst < 1e-12, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')

    r = run_family(p, 1.0, series, vg['G'], 'delta', 'real')
    expect = list(range(vg['G'], vg['T'], vg['G']))
    check('death_dates', r['deaths'] == expect, f'{r["deaths"]}')

    return checks, {'plan_s1': bench, 'flat_spread_N30': spread, 'plan_fixture_applies': applies,
                    'min_state_units': diag['min_state_units']}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P2b VALIDATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _drive(p: dict, alpha: float, V_path: list, rule: str, env: str = 'real'):
    """Run Route C holding years along an explicit true-value path (no deaths)."""
    sim_p = rate_params(p)
    led, diag = Ledger(), _new_diag()
    st = _new_state(alpha, V_path[0])
    led.post(0, 'endow', 'market', 'family_equity', V_path[0])
    for t in range(1, len(V_path)):
        _holding_year(led, t, st, V_path[t - 1], V_path[t], alpha, sim_p, env, 1.0, rule, 0.0)
        _check(led, st, V_path[t], diag)
    return st, led, diag


def _oscillation_check(p: dict, V: float = 100.0, years: int = 80) -> dict:
    """
    Plan §7 check 7. A one-off delta of V on an empty envelope, run through
    explicit annual assessments (legacy rule), against the legacy
    settle_tw_flows. Returns the two flow lists and the net tax of each.
    """
    sim_p = rate_params(p)
    led = Ledger()
    st  = _new_state(1.0, V)
    st['W'] = 0.0
    led.post(0, 'endow', 'market', 'family_equity', V)
    rc = _heir_arrival(led, 0, st, V, 1.0, sim_p, 'credited', 'delta', 1.0, 'legacy')
    flows = [rc[3]]
    for t in range(1, years + 1):
        row, _ = _holding_year(led, t, st, V, V, 1.0, sim_p, 'credited')
        flows.append(row['L'])
    _, net_leg, _, leg = settle_tw_flows({'TW': V, 'W_sell': V, 'cum_after': 0.0}, p)
    expect = tau(V, sim_p) * V                  # one-off heir tax on the whole stake (post basis)
    later = max((abs(x) for x in flows[1:]), default=0.0)
    worst = max(abs(flows[0] - expect), later, abs(net_leg), max((abs(x) for x in leg), default=0.0))
    return {'net_engine': sum(flows), 'net_legacy': net_leg, 'n_legacy_flows': len(leg),
            'max_flow_diff': worst, 'first_flows': flows[:4]}


def _p2b_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P2b checks: plan §7 checks 7 and 10, plus the refund-cap and rule-switch checks."""
    checks = {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    g      = p['g_real']
    vg     = p['val_gen']
    alphas = p['sweep']['alpha_vals']
    rho    = p['rho']
    T, G   = vg['T'], vg['G']
    ir     = _ir(p)
    series = [g] * T
    fp     = _flat(p)
    diag   = _new_diag()
    info   = {}

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            diag[key] = max(diag[key], d[key])
        diag['min_state_units'] = min(diag['min_state_units'], d['min_state_units'])

    # 7. oscillation check (legacy rule)
    o = _oscillation_check(p)
    check('c7_post_basis_one_off_heir_tax_then_zero_flows',
          o['max_flow_diff'] < 1e-9 and o['n_legacy_flows'] == 0,
          f"engine net {o['net_engine']:.6f} = tau(V) V; later and legacy flows zero (max {o['max_flow_diff']:.2e})")
    info['oscillation'] = o

    # 10. consumption identity: c = g/(1+g) keeps declared W flat -> zero delta, zero tax
    c_flat = g / (1.0 + g)
    worst_w = worst_l = 0.0
    for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
        for a in (1.0, 2.0):
            r = run_family(p, a, series, None, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c_flat, refund_rule=rule)
            absorb(r)
            for x in r['rows']:
                if x['event'] == 'year':
                    worst_w = max(worst_w, abs(x['W'] - a * p['V0_m']) / (a * p['V0_m']))
                    worst_l = max(worst_l, abs(x['L']))
    check('c10_consumption_identity_zero_delta_zero_tax', worst_w < 1e-9 and worst_l < 1e-9,
          f'max rel dW={worst_w:.2e}, max|L|={worst_l:.2e}, c={c_flat:.4%}')

    # 10b. refunds never exceed what was paid: u_out >= 0 always; state stake >= 0.
    #      Consumption above the flat-W level forces negative deltas (refunds).
    worst_u = 0.0
    legacy_net_min = 0.0
    for c in vg['consumption_vals'] + [c_flat, 0.12, 0.20]:
        for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
            for env in _ENVELOPE_UNITS:
                for a in alphas:
                    r = run_family(p, a, series, G, 'delta', env, consumption=c,
                                   index_rate=ir, refund_rule=rule)
                    absorb(r)
                    worst_u = min(worst_u, r['u_out_T'], r['s_T'])
                    if rule == 'legacy':
                        legacy_net_min = min(legacy_net_min, r['net_credited'])
    check('c10b_refund_units_never_exceed_paid', worst_u > -1e-12, f'min(u_out, s_T)={worst_u:.2e}')
    info['legacy_min_net_credited'] = legacy_net_min

    # round trip: price up 50% then back. ratio_mirror cannot return more units than paid.
    flat_up_down = [100.0, 150.0, 100.0]
    f_m, _, d_m = _drive(fp, 1.0, flat_up_down, 'ratio_mirror')
    f_l, _, d_l = _drive(fp, 1.0, flat_up_down, 'legacy')
    check('ratio_mirror_round_trip_cannot_exceed_paid',
          f_m['f'] <= 1.0 + 1e-12 and abs(f_m['f'] - (1.0 - fp['tau_0'] ** 2 / 9.0)) < 1e-9,
          f"f={f_m['f']:.6f}, hand value 1 - tau^2/9 = {1.0 - fp['tau_0'] ** 2 / 9.0:.6f}")
    info['round_trip_units'] = {'ratio_mirror': f_m['f'], 'legacy': f_l['f']}
    # mirror fractions on the first leg are exactly tau*x/(1+x) and tau*(1-1/(1+x))
    tau0 = fp['tau_0']; x = 0.5
    st1, _, _ = _drive(fp, 1.0, [100.0, 150.0], 'ratio_mirror')
    check('ratio_mirror_payment_fraction_is_tau_x_over_1_plus_x',
          abs((1.0 - st1['f']) - tau0 * x / (1.0 + x)) < 1e-12, f"{1.0 - st1['f']:.6f}")
    # a pure price fall with nothing paid refunds nothing
    st2, _, _ = _drive(fp, 1.0, [100.0, 50.0], 'ratio_mirror')
    check('ratio_mirror_no_refund_without_payment', st2['f'] == 1.0 and st2['s'] == 0.0)

    # flat rate: family stake alpha-free under every P2b switch
    worst = 0.0
    for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
        for c in (0.0, 0.035):
            for idx_r in (0.0, ir):
                fs = []
                for a in alphas:
                    r = run_family(fp, a, series, G, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c,
                                   index_rate=idx_r, refund_rule=rule)
                    absorb(r); fs.append(r['f_T'])
                worst = max(worst, max(fs) - min(fs))
    check('flat_rate_alpha_free_all_p2b_switches', worst < 1e-12, f'spread={worst:.2e}')

    # indexing lowers the rate at a given nominal W, so the honest family keeps at least as much
    worst = 1.0
    for c in (0.0, 0.035):
        for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
            a0 = run_family(p, 1.0, series, G, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c, refund_rule=rule)
            a1 = run_family(p, 1.0, series, G, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c,
                            index_rate=ir, refund_rule=rule)
            worst = min(worst, a1['f_T'] - a0['f_T'])
    check('indexing_never_raises_honest_tax', worst > -1e-12, f'min(f_idx - f_noidx)={worst:.2e}')

    # honest identity with every P2b switch on
    worst = 0.0
    for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
        m = family_pair(p, 1.0, series, G, 'delta', 'real', rho, consumption=0.035,
                        index_rate=ir, refund_rule=rule)
        worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']), abs(m['state_stake_rel'] or 0.0), abs(m['pv_rel'] or 0.0))
    check('honest_identity_p2b', worst < 1e-12)

    # consumed sink balances with the ledger
    r = run_family(p, 1.0, series, G, 'delta', 'real', consumption=0.035,
                   index_rate=ir, refund_rule='ratio_mirror')
    ent = sum(e['amount'] for e in r['ledger'].entries if e['kind'] == 'consume')
    check('consumed_sink_equals_sum_of_sales', abs(ent - r['consumed_true']) < 1e-9 * max(1.0, ent))
    absorb(r)

    check('p2b_conservation', diag['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max err={diag['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('p2b_in_kind_identity', diag['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max rel err={diag['unit_err']:.2e}")
    check('p2b_refundable_units_within_state_stake', diag['uout_err'] < 1e-12,
          f"max err={diag['uout_err']:.2e}")
    return checks, info


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P3 VALIDATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _p3_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P3 checks: plan §7 checks 3, 4, 5, 6 plus the reductions to P2 / a single asset."""
    checks, info = {}, {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    g, vg  = p['g_real'], p['val_gen']
    T, G   = vg['T'], vg['G']
    ir     = _ir(p)
    rho    = p['rho']
    alphas = p['sweep']['alpha_vals']
    ser    = [g] * T
    base   = dict(vg['route_shares'])
    cons   = vg['consumption']
    cyc    = _reset_cycles(vg)
    d3     = _p3_new_diag()

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            d3[key] = max(d3[key], d[key])
        for key in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units'):
            d3[key] = min(d3[key], d[key])
        if abs(sum(run['ledger'].bal.values())) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, run['family_true_T']):
            raise AssertionError('P3 ledger does not balance')

    # reductions
    worst = 0.0
    for c in (0.0, cons):
        for a in alphas:
            r2 = run_family(p, a, ser, G, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                            refund_rule='ratio_mirror')
            r3 = run_family3(p, a, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                             shares={'C': 1.0})
            absorb(r3)
            worst = max(worst, abs(r2['f_T'] * r2['V_T'] - r3['family_true_T']) / r3['family_true_T'])
    check('p3_C_only_equals_P2', worst < 1e-12, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')

    worst = 0.0
    for c in (0.0, cons):
        h1 = run_family(p, 1.0, ser, None, 'delta', 'real', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                        refund_rule='ratio_mirror')
        h3 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, None, 'delta', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                         shares={'A': 0.5, 'B': 0.25, 'C': 0.25})
        absorb(h3)
        worst = max(worst, abs(h1['f_T'] * h1['V_T'] - h3['family_true_T']) / h3['family_true_T'])
    check('p3_honest_ABC_equals_single_asset', worst < 1e-12, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')

    # check 3: honest identity under every route switch. A voluntary reset is an action, not a rule: an honest family that
    # resets is a different strategy, so the identity is "the honest family under the rule" = itself, whatever the rule switch.
    worst = 0.0
    for mode in _B_MODES:
        for dv in (False, True):
            for lam in (0.0, vg['lambda_base']):
                m = family3_pair(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, consumption=cons, index_rate=ir, shares=base,
                                 route_b=mode, r_def=0.025, income_ratio=0.05, death_verify=dv, verify_hazard=lam,
                                 verify_hazard_D=lam)
                worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']), abs(m['state_rel'] or 0.0), abs(m['pv_rel'] or 0.0))
    check('c3_honest_identity_all_route_switches', worst < 1e-12, f'max={worst:.2e}')

    # check 4: A/B inertness
    worst = 0.0
    for aC in alphas:
        for aD in alphas:
            m = family3_pair(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', rho, consumption=cons, index_rate=ir,
                             shares={'A': 0.6, 'B': 0.4})
            worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']))
    check('c4_AB_only_families_have_zero_gain', worst < 1e-12, f'max|gain|={worst:.2e}')

    # check 5: dilution. Only C deviates (alpha_C = 0.5); the rest is Route A.
    dil = {}
    for s in (0.02, 0.04, 0.08, 0.16):
        m = family3_pair(p, 0.5, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, consumption=cons, index_rate=ir,
                         shares={'A': 1.0 - s, 'C': s})
        dil[s] = m['gain']
    ratio = dil[0.08] / dil[0.04] if dil[0.04] != 0.0 else None
    info['dilution_gain_by_C_share'] = dil
    check('c5_dilution_roughly_linear_in_C_share',
          ratio is not None and 1.5 < ratio < 2.5, f'gain(8%)/gain(4%)={ratio}')

    # check 6: caps, over a switch grid, plus conservation
    worst_lost = 0.0
    n_runs = 0
    for c in (cons, 0.12):
        for rs in (None, cyc[0], 7):                       # no reset, and the family's own voluntary reset cycles
            for aC in (0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0):
                for aD in (0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0):
                    r = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                                    shares=base, reset=rs)
                    absorb(r); n_runs += 1
                    worst_lost = max(worst_lost, r['lost_refund'])
    check('c6_refunds_never_exceed_paid_units_or_value',
          d3['min_E_cash'] > -1e-9 and d3['min_A_D'] > -1e-12 and d3['min_u_out'] > -1e-12
          and d3['min_state_units'] > -1e-12 and d3['uout_err'] < 1e-12,
          f"{n_runs} runs; min E_cash={d3['min_E_cash']:.2e}, min A_D={d3['min_A_D']:.2e}, "
          f"min u_out={d3['min_u_out']:.2e}")
    check('p3_conservation', d3['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max err={d3['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('p3_in_kind_identity', d3['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max rel err={d3['unit_err']:.2e}")
    info['max_lost_refund_gbp_m'] = worst_lost

    # a voluntary reset bounds Route D understatement (finding, asserted as a direction). The honest baseline never resets.
    opts = dict(consumption=cons, index_rate=ir, shares=base)
    hn = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **opts)
    g_reset = family3_pair(p, 1.0, 0.5, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=hn, own={'reset': cyc[0]}, **opts)['gain']
    g_never = family3_pair(p, 1.0, 0.5, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=hn, **opts)['gain']
    info['D_understate_gain_alpha_D_0.5'] = {'reset': g_reset, 'never': g_never, 'cycle': cyc[0]}
    check('voluntary_reset_reduces_route_D_understatement_gain', g_reset < g_never,
          f'gain with a reset every {cyc[0]}y {g_reset:+.4f}, never {g_never:+.4f}')
    return checks, info


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P4 VALIDATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _first_year_at(share_by_year: list, threshold: float):
    """First year t (1-indexed) at which the verified share reaches `threshold`, else None."""
    for i, v_ in enumerate(share_by_year, start=1):
        if v_ >= threshold:
            return i
    return None


def _p4_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P4 checks: plan §7 check 8 (lambda -> 0), honest identity and inertness under lambda,
    the verified-share law, conservation with the verified tranche, and direction."""
    checks, info = {}, {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    g, vg  = p['g_real'], p['val_gen']
    T, G   = vg['T'], vg['G']
    ir     = _ir(p) if vg['index_wmin'] else 0.0
    rho    = p['rho']
    ser    = [g] * T
    base   = dict(vg['route_shares'])
    cons   = vg['consumption']
    lams   = [x for x in vg['lambda_vals'] if x > 0.0]
    opts   = dict(consumption=cons, index_rate=ir, shares=base)
    d4     = _p3_new_diag()

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            d4[key] = max(d4[key], d[key])
        for key in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units'):
            d4[key] = min(d4[key], d[key])
        if abs(sum(run['ledger'].bal.values())) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, run['family_true_T']):
            raise AssertionError('P4 ledger does not balance')

    # 8. lambda -> 0 continuity: a vanishing hazard reproduces the no-verification result
    worst = 0.0
    for aC in (0.1, 0.5, 2.0):
        for aD in (0.5, 1.0):
            a0 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', **opts)
            a1 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', verify_hazard=1e-9, **opts)
            absorb(a1)
            worst = max(worst, abs(a1['family_true_T'] - a0['family_true_T']) / a0['family_true_T'])
    check('c8_lambda_to_zero_reproduces_no_verification', worst < 1e-6, f'max rel diff at lambda=1e-9: {worst:.2e}')

    # honest identity and inertness: with alpha_C = 1 verification changes nothing
    worst_gain = worst_inert = 0.0
    for lam in lams + [1.0]:
        m = family3_pair(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, verify_hazard=lam, **opts)
        worst_gain = max(worst_gain, abs(m['gain']), abs(m['state_rel'] or 0.0), abs(m['pv_rel'] or 0.0))
        for aD in (0.5, 2.0):
            r0 = run_family3(p, 1.0, aD, ser, G, 'delta', **opts)
            r1 = run_family3(p, 1.0, aD, ser, G, 'delta', verify_hazard=lam, **opts)
            absorb(r1)
            worst_inert = max(worst_inert, abs(r1['family_true_T'] - r0['family_true_T']) / r0['family_true_T'])
    check('c3_honest_identity_under_lambda', worst_gain < 1e-12, f'max={worst_gain:.2e}')
    check('verification_inert_when_alpha_C_is_1', worst_inert < 1e-9, f'max rel diff={worst_inert:.2e}')

    # verified-share law: 1 - (1 - lambda)^t, exact without consumption
    worst = 0.0
    for lam in lams + [1.0]:
        r = run_family3(p, 0.5, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', consumption=0.0, index_rate=ir, shares=base,
                        verify_hazard=lam)
        absorb(r)
        yr = [x['t'] for x in r['rows'] if 'verified_share' in x]
        for t, v_ in zip(yr, r['verified_share']):
            worst = max(worst, abs(v_ - (1.0 - (1.0 - lam) ** t)))
    check('verified_share_equals_1_minus_(1-lambda)^t', worst < 1e-12, f'max|diff|={worst:.2e}')

    # A/B inertness and no-C inertness
    worst = 0.0
    for lam in lams:
        for aC in (0.1, 2.0):
            m = family3_pair(p, aC, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, verify_hazard=lam,
                             **dict(opts, shares={'A': 0.6, 'B': 0.4}))
            worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']))
    check('c4_no_C_families_ignore_lambda', worst < 1e-12, f'max|gain|={worst:.2e}')

    # caps and conservation with the verified tranche, over a switch grid
    n_runs = 0
    for lam in lams + [1.0]:
        for c in (cons, 0.12):
            for rs in (None, _reset_cycles(vg)[0]):
                for aC in (0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0):
                    for aD in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0):
                        r = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', consumption=c, index_rate=ir,
                                        shares=base, reset=rs, verify_hazard=lam, verify_hazard_D=lam)
                        absorb(r); n_runs += 1
    check('c6_caps_hold_with_verified_tranche',
          d4['min_E_cash'] > -1e-9 and d4['min_A_D'] > -1e-12 and d4['min_u_out'] > -1e-12
          and d4['min_state_units'] > -1e-12 and d4['uout_err'] < 1e-12,
          f"{n_runs} runs; min u_out={d4['min_u_out']:.2e}, min state units={d4['min_state_units']:.2e}")
    check('p4_conservation', d4['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max err={d4['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('p4_in_kind_identity', d4['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max rel err={d4['unit_err']:.2e}")

    # direction: with a C-heavy mix, verification takes the understatement gain away
    heavy = dict(opts, shares={'A': 0.5, 'C': 0.5})
    gains = {}
    for lam in [0.0] + lams:
        h = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', verify_hazard=lam, **heavy)
        gains[lam] = family3_pair(p, 0.5, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=h,
                                  verify_hazard=lam, **heavy)['gain']
    ordered = [gains[x] for x in sorted(gains)]
    info['C_heavy_gain_by_lambda_alpha_C_0.5'] = gains
    check('verification_erodes_understatement_gain_C_heavy',
          all(ordered[i + 1] < ordered[i] + 1e-12 for i in range(len(ordered) - 1)) and ordered[-1] < ordered[0],
          '; '.join(f'{x:.0%}: {gains[x]:+.2%}' for x in sorted(gains)))
    return checks, info


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P5 — STRATEGY SEARCH AND BRG/HSC/SPT/SST VERDICTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

_DEFAULTS = {'b_shift': (0.5, 1.0),            # share of Route B moved into D (or C) by a route-migration strategy; overridden by [val_gen] b_shift once load_params passes it
             'reset_cycles': (5, 10, 20)}      # used only when [val_gen] reset_sens holds no positive cycle


def _reset_cycles(vg: dict) -> list:
    """Voluntary Route D reset cycles (years) a family may choose. [val_gen] reset_sens is read as a menu of STRATEGY cycles, not a rule."""
    cyc = [int(m) for m in (vg.get('reset_sens') or []) if int(m) > 0]
    return cyc or list(_DEFAULTS['reset_cycles'])


def _strategies(p: dict, grid: list | None = None) -> list:
    """
    Declaration strategies (plan §5), each a dict with the Route C / Route D declaration ratios (numbers or functions of
    ctx) and, where the strategy needs one, the family's OWN reset cycle, Route B election or route migration:
      constant              every year, full (alpha_C, alpha_D) grid
      first_gen_only        deviate in generation 0, honest afterwards
      late_deviation        deviate in the final k years before each death (and before T)
      correct_before_death  deviate until k years before each death, then honest
      voluntary_reset       the family resets Route D every m years (an action, D6): D at a constant ratio (a = 1 is a
                            pure honest reset), or C and D together
      pre_reset_deviation   Route D deviates in the k years before the family's own reset (cycle m)
      reset_gaming          Route D declared high (a) before the family's reset and low (1/a) after
      b_election            Route B: elect the lien or the income mode instead of the rule's default (honest declarations)
      route_shift           Route B: move a share s of Route B into D (or C) and understate it (route shopping)
    Targets: C, D, CD (the same pattern on both), B, BD, BC. Honest (1, 1) with no action is excluded.
    """
    vg   = p['val_gen']
    if grid is None:        # the library of record; a custom grid gives a single-level slice (HLC)
        grid = sorted(set(p['sweep']['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext']))
    al    = [a for a in grid if a != 1.0]
    over  = [a for a in al if a > 1.0]
    under = [a for a in al if a < 1.0]
    ks    = vg['strategy_k']
    cyc   = _reset_cycles(vg)
    out   = []
    for aC in grid:
        for aD in grid:
            if aC == 1.0 and aD == 1.0:
                continue
            out.append({'name': 'constant', 'target': 'CD', 'a': (aC, aD), 'k': None,
                        'aC': aC, 'aD': aD, 'cycle': 0})

    def add(name, kk, avals, targets, pattern, cycles=(0,)):
        for m in cycles:
            for k in kk:
                if m and k is not None and k >= m:      # a window as long as the cycle is just "always deviate"
                    continue
                for a in avals:
                    for tg in targets:
                        f = pattern(a, k)
                        st = {'name': name, 'target': tg, 'a': a, 'k': k, 'cycle': m,
                              'aC': f if 'C' in tg else 1.0, 'aD': f if 'D' in tg else 1.0}
                        if m:
                            st['reset'] = m
                        out.append(st)

    add('first_gen_only', [None], al, ('C', 'D', 'CD'),
        lambda a, k: (lambda c: a if c['gen'] == 0 else 1.0))
    add('late_deviation', ks, al, ('C', 'D', 'CD'),
        lambda a, k: (lambda c: a if c['yrs_to_death'] < k else 1.0))
    add('correct_before_death', ks, al, ('C', 'D', 'CD'),
        lambda a, k: (lambda c: a if c['yrs_to_death'] >= k else 1.0))
    for m in cyc:
        for a in grid:
            out.append({'name': 'voluntary_reset', 'target': 'D', 'a': a, 'k': None, 'aC': 1.0, 'aD': a,
                        'cycle': m, 'reset': m})
        for a in al:
            out.append({'name': 'voluntary_reset', 'target': 'CD', 'a': a, 'k': None, 'aC': a, 'aD': a,
                        'cycle': m, 'reset': m})
    add('pre_reset_deviation', ks, al, ('D',),
        lambda a, k: (lambda c: a if c['yrs_to_reset'] < k else 1.0), cyc)
    add('reset_gaming', ks, over, ('D',),
        lambda a, k: (lambda c: a if c['yrs_to_reset'] < k else 1.0 / a), cyc)
    # Route B strategies
    rb = p.get('route_b') or {}
    base_mode = rb.get('payment_mode', 'sale')
    ph2 = _phase2_opts(p)
    for mode in _B_MODES:
        if mode == base_mode or (mode == 'income' and ph2.get('income_ratio', 0.0) <= 0.0):
            continue                                    # no income to pay from: the same as the default mode
        out.append({'name': 'b_election', 'target': 'B', 'a': mode, 'k': None, 'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0,
                    'cycle': 0, 'route_b': mode})
    if vg['route_shares'].get('B', 0.0) > 0.0:
        for s in (vg.get('b_shift') or _DEFAULTS['b_shift']):
            for a in under:
                out.append({'name': 'route_shift', 'target': 'BD', 'a': a, 'k': None, 'aC': 1.0, 'aD': a,
                            'cycle': 0, 'shift': ('B', 'D', s)})
                out.append({'name': 'route_shift', 'target': 'BC', 'a': a, 'k': None, 'aC': a, 'aD': 1.0,
                            'cycle': 0, 'shift': ('B', 'C', s)})
    return out


def _label(st: dict) -> str:
    if st['name'] == 'constant':
        return f"constant C={st['a'][0]} D={st['a'][1]}"
    k = '' if st['k'] is None else f" k={st['k']}"
    m = f" m={st['cycle']}" if st.get('cycle') else ''
    sh = f" s={st['shift'][2]}" if st.get('shift') else ''
    return f"{st['name']} {st['target']} a={st['a']}{k}{m}{sh}"


def _own(st: dict, shares: dict) -> dict:
    """The switches that belong to a strategy and not to the rule set: its reset, Route B election and route migration."""
    own = {}
    if st.get('reset'):
        own['reset'] = st['reset']
    if st.get('route_b'):
        own['route_b'] = st['route_b']
    if st.get('shift'):
        src, dst, s = st['shift']
        sh = dict(shares)
        mv = sh.get(src, 0.0) * s
        sh[src] = sh.get(src, 0.0) - mv
        sh[dst] = sh.get(dst, 0.0) + mv
        own['shares'] = sh
    return own


def _line(st: dict, shares: dict) -> dict:
    """A strategy as one line of run_batch."""
    return {'aC': st['aC'], 'aD': st['aD'], **_own(st, shares)}


_BASE_RULE = 'units'                          # no value cap, no corrective auction
_CANDIDATE_RULE = 'units_and_value/reset/on'  # the simple universal rule


def _phase2_opts(p):
    """Phase 2 switches from the parameter file ([route_b], [income], [verification]); empty if absent.
    p['archetype'] (set by _p6_archetypes) selects the external-income ratio from [income.by_archetype]."""
    rb, inc, ver = p.get('route_b'), p.get('income'), p.get('verification')
    out = {}
    if rb:
        out.update(route_b=rb['payment_mode'], r_def=rb['r_def'])
    if inc:
        out.update(income_ratio=inc['by_archetype'].get(p.get('archetype'), inc['default_ratio']),
                   income_cap=inc['cap'])
    if ver:
        out.update(death_verify=ver['death_verifies'])
    return out


def _lam_D(p: dict, lam_C: float) -> float:
    """The corrective-auction hazard lambda_D paired with a lambda_C in the headline grids: [verification] lambda_D when it is
    positive (a fixed, independent value), else equal to lambda_C (the coupling of the earlier engine, kept so the grids are
    comparable). The independent lambda_C x lambda_D grid is p3_lambda_grid."""
    ver = p.get('verification') or {}
    return ver['lambda_D'] if ver.get('lambda_D', 0.0) > 0.0 else lam_C


def _p5_opts(p, rule, lam, lam_D=None):
    """`rule` is a rule-set key 'c_cap/verify_down/dauc' (see the module header, RULE SETS);
    trailing parts may be omitted and take the defaults units / allow / off. `lam` is lambda_C, the Route C verification
    hazard. lambda_D (the Route D corrective auction, active when dauc = on) is `lam_D`, else _lam_D(p, lam).
    The scheduled Route D reset and the death waiver are retired: nothing here is a reset clock."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    parts = rule.split('/')
    cap = parts[0]
    verify_down = parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else 'allow'
    dauc = parts[2] if len(parts) > 2 else 'off'
    ld = (lam_D if lam_D is not None else _lam_D(p, lam)) if dauc == 'on' else 0.0
    return dict(consumption=vg['consumption'],
                index_rate=_ir(p) if vg['index_wmin'] else 0.0,
                shares=vg['route_shares'], verify_hazard=lam, c_cap=cap,
                verify_down=verify_down, verify_hazard_D=ld,
                **_phase2_opts(p))


def _p5_search(p: dict, rule: str, lam: float, strategies: list, ser: list | None = None,
               lam_D: float | None = None) -> dict:
    """Best response and BRG / SPT / SST verdict for one (rule set, lambda_C, lambda_D). The whole library runs as one batch."""
    vg  = p['val_gen']
    ser = list(ser) if ser is not None else [p['g_real']] * vg['T']     # a JST replay path, else constant real g
    tol = vg['state_tol']
    o   = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam, lam_D)
    lines = [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [_line(st, o['shares']) for st in strategies]
    B = run_batch(p, lines, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], rhos=_rhos(p), **o)
    recs = []
    for i, st in enumerate(strategies, start=1):
        m = _batch_metrics(p, B, i, 0)
        recs.append({'label': _label(st), 'name': st['name'], 'target': st['target'],
                     'gain': m['gain'], 'pv_rel': m['pv_rel'], 'state_rel': m['state_rel'],
                     'pv_rel_by_rho': m['pv_rel_by_rho']})
    best = max(recs, key=lambda r_: r_['gain'])
    gaining = [r_ for r_ in recs if r_['gain'] > 0.0]

    def bad_pv(r_):
        return r_['pv_rel'] is None or abs(r_['pv_rel']) > tol

    def bad_st(r_):
        return r_['state_rel'] is None or abs(r_['state_rel']) > tol

    conf_pv = [r_ for r_ in gaining if bad_pv(r_)]
    conf_st = [r_ for r_ in gaining if bad_st(r_)]
    conf_any = [r_ for r_ in gaining if bad_pv(r_) or bad_st(r_)]
    conf = list(conf_st)       # D1c: SST (discount-free) is the primary state test; n_conflict counts SST conflicts
    conf.sort(key=lambda r_: -r_['gain'])
    spt_by_rho = {}
    for rk_ in (p.get('rho_sens') or []):
        bad_ = [x_ for x_ in gaining if x_['pv_rel_by_rho'].get(str(rk_)) is None or abs(x_['pv_rel_by_rho'][str(rk_)]) > tol]
        spt_by_rho[str(rk_)] = {'n_conflict': len(bad_), 'pass': len(bad_) == 0}
    by_family = {}
    for r_ in recs:
        k_ = r_['name']
        if k_ not in by_family or r_['gain'] > by_family[k_]['gain']:
            by_family[k_] = r_

    def _extreme(key):
        pool = [r_ for r_ in gaining if r_[key] is not None]
        if not pool:
            return None
        w = max(pool, key=lambda r_: abs(r_[key]))
        return {'label': w['label'], 'gain': w['gain'], 'value': w[key]}

    by_cycle = {}
    for r_, st in zip(recs, strategies):
        k_ = str(st.get('cycle', 0))
        if k_ not in by_cycle or r_['gain'] > by_cycle[k_]['gain']:
            by_cycle[k_] = {'gain': r_['gain'], 'label': r_['label']}
    return {'rule': rule, 'lambda': lam, 'lambda_D': o['verify_hazard_D'], 'n_strategies': len(recs), 'best_by_cycle': by_cycle,
            'worst_pv': _extreme('pv_rel'), 'worst_state': _extreme('state_rel'),
            'best': best, 'BRG_pass': best['gain'] <= vg['brg_tol'],
            'n_gaining': len(gaining), 'n_conflict': len(conf), 'n_conflict_any': len(conf_any),
            'n_conflict_spt': len(conf_pv), 'n_conflict_sst': len(conf_st),
            'worst_conflicts': conf[:5], 'SPT_pass': len(conf_pv) == 0, 'SST_pass': len(conf_st) == 0,
            'spt_by_rho': spt_by_rho, 'state_test': 'SST',
            'best_by_family': by_family, 'all': recs}


def _honest_shock_cost(p: dict, rule: str, lam: float | None = None) -> tuple:
    """
    HSC: what the rule costs an HONEST family that makes honest valuation errors and is then hit by a genuine market fall.
    The earlier proxy ran an error-free honest family, for which verification and the corrective auction are inert, so the
    test could not fail. Here each family values Routes C and D with a multiplicative AR(1) error of sd sigma (hec_sigmas > 0,
    the HEC paths, zero bias) and the market falls by `shock` in shock_year. cost(rule) = mean over paths of
    TW(error path) / TW(error-free honest) - 1 under that rule; the HSC figure is cost(rule) - cost(base rule), the extra
    cost the rule puts on honest families that err, taken at the worst sigma. lambda_C = lambda_D defaults to lambda_base.
    Returns ({shock: figure}, {shock: {sigma: {rule, base, extra}}}).
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    lam = vg['lambda_base'] if lam is None else lam
    sigmas = [s for s in vg['hec_sigmas'] if s > 0.0]
    out, detail = {}, {}
    for shock in vg['shock_sizes']:
        ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
        ser[vg['shock_year'] - 1] = shock
        per = {}
        for sg in sigmas:
            lines = [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [
                {'aC': (lambda c, pc=pc: pc[c['t']]), 'aD': (lambda c, pd=pd: pd[c['t']])}
                for pc, pd in _hec_paths(vg, sg, vg['hec_seed'])]
            cost = {}
            for key, r_ in (('rule', rule), ('base', _BASE_RULE)):
                B = run_batch(p, lines, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **_p5_opts(p, r_, lam))
                cost[key] = float(np.mean(B['family_true_T'][1:] / B['family_true_T'][0] - 1.0))
            per[str(sg)] = dict(cost, extra=cost['rule'] - cost['base'])
        out[str(shock)] = min((v['extra'] for v in per.values()), default=0.0)
        detail[str(shock)] = per
    return out, detail


def _gains_batch(p: dict, rule: str, lam: float, ser: list, strategies: list, shares: dict | None = None,
                 lam_D: float | None = None) -> tuple:
    """Metrics of every strategy against the honest family on `ser`, one batch. Returns (list of metric dicts, options used)."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam, lam_D)
    if shares is not None:
        o['shares'] = shares
    lines = [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [_line(st, o['shares']) for st in strategies]
    B = run_batch(p, lines, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], rhos=_rhos(p), **o)
    return [_batch_metrics(p, B, i, 0) for i in range(1, len(strategies) + 1)], o


def _conventional_run(p: dict, alpha_C: float, alpha_D: float, rate: float) -> dict:
    """
    Reference system for the "no clear unbounded strategy" claim: a conventional self-declared
    wealth tax. Every year the family pays `rate` x DECLARED value, in kind at the true price
    (so units paid = rate x alpha x units held). Routes A/B are professionally valued (alpha = 1);
    C and D are declared at alpha_C, alpha_D. No delta, no refund, no verification, no auction,
    no reset; same growth, consumption, route shares and horizon as the WDT runs. Deaths change
    nothing (no tax event). Returns terminal family true value and the PV of the state's receipts.
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    T = vg['T']
    alpha = {'A': 1.0, 'B': 1.0, 'C': alpha_C, 'D': alpha_D}
    tw = pv = 0.0
    for r, sh in vg['route_shares'].items():
        f, V = 1.0, sh * p['V0_m']
        for t in range(1, T + 1):
            V *= 1.0 + p['g_real']
            f -= f * vg['consumption']
            units = rate * alpha[r] * f
            f -= units
            pv += units * V / (1.0 + p['rho']) ** t
        tw += f * V
    return {'TW': tw, 'PV': pv}


def _conventional_rate(p: dict, target_tw: float) -> float:
    """Flat rate at which the honest conventional family ends with the same terminal true wealth as
    the honest WDT family, i.e. carries the same tax burden. (Equal present value of receipts is not
    attainable: with growth above the discount rate, PV peaks at a modest rate and then falls.)"""
    lo, hi = 0.0, 0.99
    for _ in range(200):
        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
        if _conventional_run(p, 1.0, 1.0, mid)['TW'] > target_tw:
            lo = mid
        else:
            hi = mid
    return 0.5 * (lo + hi)


def _p5_conventional(p: dict, strategies_alphas: list, rate: float | None = None) -> dict:
    """
    Best response against the conventional system, for comparison with the WDT search. The
    flat rate is calibrated so the honest family ends with the same terminal wealth as under the WDT
    (candidate rule, lambda = 0), i.e. the same burden on honest families. Gain = TW(a)/TW(honest) - 1 over the (alpha_C, alpha_D) grid.
    With `rate` given (the HLC pair: a RATES burden) the calibration is skipped and target_tw is None.
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    if rate is None:
        h_wdt = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **_p5_opts(p, _CANDIDATE_RULE, 0.0))
        target = h_wdt['family_true_T']
        rate = _conventional_rate(p, target)
    else:
        target = None
    h = _conventional_run(p, 1.0, 1.0, rate)
    cells = {}
    for aC in strategies_alphas:
        for aD in strategies_alphas:
            cells[f'{aC}|{aD}'] = _conventional_run(p, aC, aD, rate)['TW'] / h['TW'] - 1.0
    best_k = max(cells, key=cells.get)
    full = _conventional_run(p, 0.0, 0.0, rate)['TW'] / h['TW'] - 1.0
    return {'rate': rate, 'target_tw': target, 'honest_TW': h['TW'], 'cells': cells,
            'best': {'key': best_k, 'gain': cells[best_k]},
            'full_understatement_gain': full,
            'diag_alpha': {str(a): cells[f'{a}|{a}'] for a in strategies_alphas}}


def _p5_no_tax_tw(p: dict) -> float:
    """Terminal family true wealth with no tax at all (flat, negligible rate)."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    p0 = dict(p, tau_0=1e-12, tau_m=1e-12, schedule='logistic')
    return run_family3(p0, 1.0, 1.0, [p['g_real']] * vg['T'], vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'],
                       **_p5_opts(p0, _BASE_RULE, 0.0))['family_true_T']


def _p5_upper_bound(p: dict, rule: str, lam: float, tw_no_tax: float) -> float:
    """
    Strategy-free ceiling on any family's gain under `rule` at `lam`. Tax only moves value from
    family to state and refunds are capped by what was paid, so no declaration strategy can leave
    the family richer than a run with no tax: gain <= TW(no tax) / TW(honest) - 1, the honest
    family's whole tax drag as a share of its terminal wealth. main() checks it against every
    best response (a violation means a cap or a ledger leak).
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    h = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, [p['g_real']] * vg['T'], vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **_p5_opts(p, rule, lam))
    return tw_no_tax / h['family_true_T'] - 1.0


def _p5_growth_surface(p: dict, rules: list, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """
    Best-response gain over the growth rate g and the verification hazard lambda, for each rule
    in `rules`. Reads: how much room a declaration strategy has when the asset grows at g and a
    share lambda of such assets is verified each year. Slow growers have little delta to
    misdeclare; fast growers that never list are the exposed corner. Growth and lambda are
    independent inputs here (the model has no link between them). Gain is the share of the
    honest family's terminal wealth, so it is a percentage, not pounds; honest_TW_m gives scale.
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    out = {}
    for rule in rules:
        out[rule] = {}
        for g_ in vg['growth_vals']:
            pg = dict(p)
            pg['g_real'] = g_
            o = _p5_opts(pg, rule, 0.0)
            h = run_family3(pg, 1.0, 1.0, [g_] * vg['T'], vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **o)
            cells = {}
            for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
                r_ = _p5_search(pg, rule, lam, strategies)
                cells[str(lam)] = {'gain': r_['best']['gain'], 'label': r_['best']['label'],
                                   'BRG': r_['BRG_pass'], 'SPT': r_['SPT_pass'], 'SST': r_['SST_pass'],
                                   'n_conflict': r_['n_conflict']}
            out[rule][str(g_)] = {'honest_TW_m': h['family_true_T'], 'by_lambda': cells}
    return out


def _p5_dmg(p: dict, rules: list, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """
    DMG: dominance grid (NDS). A strategy dominates when its family gain over honest is
    positive in EVERY scenario. Scenarios: growth g x lambda (constant growth), and a genuine
    one-year market fall (shock_sizes at shock_year, base g) x lambda. The honest family runs
    under the same rule set and scenario. Per rule: for every strategy the minimum, mean and
    share of scenarios with a gain; the summary counts strategies that gain everywhere and
    reports the maximin strategy (highest worst-case gain).
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    scen = []
    for g_ in vg['growth_vals']:
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            scen.append(('growth', g_, lam, [g_] * vg['T']))
    for sh in vg['shock_sizes']:
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
            ser[vg['shock_year'] - 1] = sh
            scen.append(('shock', sh, lam, ser))
    out = {}
    for rule in rules:
        gains = [[] for _ in strategies]
        for kind, x_, lam, ser in scen:
            pg = dict(p)
            if kind == 'growth':
                pg['g_real'] = x_
            ms, _ = _gains_batch(pg, rule, lam, ser, strategies)
            for i, m in enumerate(ms):
                gains[i].append(m['gain'])
        recs = []
        for st, gl in zip(strategies, gains):
            recs.append({'label': _label(st), 'name': st['name'], 'target': st['target'],
                         'min_gain': min(gl), 'mean_gain': sum(gl) / len(gl),
                         'share_gaining': sum(1 for x_ in gl if x_ > 0.0) / len(gl)})
        dom = sorted([r_ for r_ in recs if r_['min_gain'] > 0.0], key=lambda r_: -r_['min_gain'])
        n_mat = sum(1 for r_ in recs if r_['min_gain'] > vg['brg_tol'])
        maximin = max(recs, key=lambda r_: r_['min_gain'])
        top = sorted(recs, key=lambda r_: -r_['share_gaining'])[:10]
        out[rule] = {'n_scenarios': len(scen), 'n_strategies': len(recs),
                     'n_dominant': len(dom), 'n_dominant_material': n_mat, 'material_threshold': vg['brg_tol'], 'dominant': dom[:10],
                     'maximin': maximin, 'top_share': top,
                     'max_share_gaining': max(r_['share_gaining'] for r_ in recs)}
    return out


def _hec_paths(vg: dict, sigma: float, seed: int) -> list:
    """Multiplicative honest valuation error on Routes C and D: declared ratio exp(e_t), e an AR(1) in logs
    with persistence hec_phi_C / hec_phi_D (both default to hec_phi) and stationary sd sigma, centred so
    E[exp(e)] = 1 (no bias, by decision of 5 Oct 2026). Independent paths for C and D.
    Deterministic given the seed (random.Random, no numpy)."""
    import random
    rng = random.Random(seed)
    phis = (vg.get('hec_phi_C', vg['hec_phi']), vg.get('hec_phi_D', vg['hec_phi']))
    out = []
    for _ in range(vg['hec_paths']):
        pair = []
        for _r in range(2):
            phi = phis[_r]
            innov = math.sqrt(max(1.0 - phi * phi, 0.0)) * sigma
            e, ser = rng.gauss(0.0, sigma), []
            for _t in range(vg['T'] + 1):
                ser.append(math.exp(e - 0.5 * sigma * sigma))
                e = phi * e + innov * rng.gauss(0.0, 1.0)
            pair.append(ser)
        out.append(pair)
    return out


def _p5_hec(p: dict, rules: list, lams: list) -> dict:
    """
    HEC: honest families that value Routes C and D with error. Error-free honest is the reference, so
    gain < 0 is the cost of honest error. Per (rule, lambda, sigma): mean and 5th / 95th percentile over
    hec_paths of the family gain (cost), pv_rel (SPT) and state_rel (SST), and the share of paths that
    gain. sigma = 0 is the honest family itself (all zero).
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    out = {}
    def pct(xs, q):
        xs = sorted(xs)
        return xs[min(len(xs) - 1, max(0, int(round(q * (len(xs) - 1)))))]
    for rule in rules:
        for lam in lams:
            o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam)
            for sg in vg['hec_sigmas']:
                paths = _hec_paths(vg, sg, vg['hec_seed'])
                lines = [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [
                    {'aC': (lambda c, pc=pc: pc[c['t']]), 'aD': (lambda c, pd=pd: pd[c['t']])} for pc, pd in paths]
                B = run_batch(p, lines, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], rhos=_rhos(p), **o)
                gs, pvs, sts = [], [], []
                for i in range(1, len(lines)):
                    m = _batch_metrics(p, B, i, 0)
                    gs.append(m['gain'])
                    if m['pv_rel'] is not None:
                        pvs.append(m['pv_rel'])
                    if m['state_rel'] is not None:
                        sts.append(m['state_rel'])
                mean = lambda xs: sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else None
                out[f'{rule}|{lam}|{sg}'] = {
                    'rule': rule, 'lambda': lam, 'sigma': sg, 'n_paths': len(gs),
                    'gain_mean': mean(gs), 'gain_p05': pct(gs, 0.05), 'gain_p95': pct(gs, 0.95),
                    'share_gaining': sum(1 for x_ in gs if x_ > 0.0) / len(gs),
                    'pv_mean': mean(pvs), 'pv_p05': pct(pvs, 0.05) if pvs else None, 'pv_p95': pct(pvs, 0.95) if pvs else None,
                    'state_mean': mean(sts), 'state_p05': pct(sts, 0.05) if sts else None, 'state_p95': pct(sts, 0.95) if sts else None}
    return out


def _direction(st: dict) -> str:
    """under | over | mixed | none, from the deviating declaration ratios of a strategy. `none`: no misdeclaration (an honest
    voluntary reset, a Route B election)."""
    if isinstance(st['a'], str):
        return 'none'
    if st['name'] == 'constant':
        devs = [a for a in st['a'] if a != 1.0]
    elif st['name'] == 'reset_gaming':
        return 'mixed'
    else:
        devs = [st['a']] if st['a'] != 1.0 else []
    if not devs:
        return 'none'
    if all(a < 1.0 for a in devs):
        return 'under'
    if all(a > 1.0 for a in devs):
        return 'over'
    return 'mixed'


def _p5_direction(p: dict, rules: list, lams: list, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """
    UOS: understatement against overstatement (evidence standard, D10), swept over the Route C share
    (c_share_vals; A absorbs the difference). Per (rule, lambda, C share): the best gain among strategies
    that only understate, only overstate, or mix both, with the strategy label, and the largest
    state_rel / pv_rel among gaining strategies of each direction.
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    sh0 = vg['route_shares']
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    out = {}
    for cs in vg['c_share_vals']:
        sh = dict(sh0)
        sh['A'] = sh0['A'] - (cs - sh0['C'])
        sh['C'] = cs
        for rule in rules:
            for lam in lams:
                ms, _ = _gains_batch(p, rule, lam, ser, strategies, shares=sh)
                best = {}
                for st, m in zip(strategies, ms):
                    d = _direction(st)
                    b = best.get(d)
                    if b is None or m['gain'] > b['gain']:
                        best[d] = {'gain': m['gain'], 'label': _label(st), 'state_rel': m['state_rel'],
                                   'pv_rel': m['pv_rel']}
                out[f'{rule}|{lam}|{cs}'] = {'rule': rule, 'lambda': lam, 'c_share': cs, 'best': best}
    return out


def _life_results(p: dict) -> dict:
    """
    LIFE step (single life, Route C, G = 1 case of the same engine). Replaces the legacy val_core heatmaps and
    N sweep. Metrics: GAIN (tw_gap, + = family retains more than honest), net_pct and pv_pct, all on the
    honest terminal wealth TW(1). Grids from [sweep]. Worked examples run through run_life, inputs in
    [val_gen.life_examples].
    """
    sw, vg = p['sweep'], p['val_gen']
    N, rho = p['N_val'], p['rho']
    out = {'N': N, 'g0': p['g_real'], 'alphas': sw['alpha_vals'], 'g_vals': sw['g_vals'],
           'n_vals': sw['n_actual_vals'], 'rhos': p['rho_sweep'], 'rho': rho}
    def cell(alpha, g, n, h, r=rho):
        series = [g] * n
        m = pair(p, alpha, series, g, r, honest=h)
        return {'gain': m['tw_gap'], 'net': m['net_pct'], 'pv': m['pv_pct'], 'pv_rel': m['pv_rel']}
    grid = {}
    for g in sw['g_vals']:
        h = run_life(p, 1.0, [g] * N, g)
        for a in sw['alpha_vals']:
            grid[f'{a}|{g}'] = cell(a, g, N, h)
    out['grid'] = grid
    by_n = {}
    for n in sw['n_actual_vals']:
        h = run_life(p, 1.0, [p['g_real']] * n, p['g_real'])
        for a in sw['alpha_vals']:
            by_n[f'{a}|{n}'] = cell(a, p['g_real'], n, h)
    out['by_n'] = by_n
    by_rho = {}
    for g in sw['g_vals']:
        h = run_life(p, 1.0, [g] * N, g)
        for a in sw['alpha_vals']:
            for r in p['rho_sweep']:
                by_rho[f'{a}|{g}|{r}'] = pair(p, a, [g] * N, g, r, honest=h)['pv_pct']
    out['by_rho'] = by_rho
    ex = {}
    for name, spec in vg['life_examples'].items():
        pe = dict(p)
        pe['V0_m'] = float(spec['V0_m'])
        runs = {}
        for a in spec['alphas']:
            r = run_life(pe, float(a), [float(spec['g'])] * int(spec['N']), float(spec['g']))
            runs[str(a)] = {'TW_settled': r['TW_settled'], 'Net_settled': r['Net_settled'],
                            'hold_true': r['hold_true'], 'sell_L': r['sell_L'], 'settle_net': r['settle_net'],
                            'rows': r['rows']}
        ex[name] = {'g': spec['g'], 'N': spec['N'], 'V0_m': spec['V0_m'], 'alphas': spec['alphas'], 'runs': runs}
    out['examples'] = ex
    return out


def _route_d_examples(p: dict) -> dict:
    """
    Worked examples L (Route D against annual settlement) and M (voluntary settlement) run through the
    family engine with a single route (share 1.0), no death event (G = None: terminal settlement at the end of
    the horizon). Inputs in [val_gen.route_d_examples.L|M]. The auction cost in M is an input applied to the
    reset value outside the engine (the engine has no auction cost).
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    ex = vg['route_d_examples']
    out = {}
    L = ex['L']
    pe = dict(p); pe['V0_m'] = float(L['V0_m'])
    ser = [float(L['g'])] * int(L['N'])
    ra = run_family3(pe, 1.0, 1.0, ser, None, vg['heir_influx'], shares={'A': 1.0})
    rd = run_family3(pe, 1.0, 1.0, ser, None, vg['heir_influx'], shares={'D': 1.0})
    V, rows, cum = float(L['V0_m']), [], 0.0
    for row, rw in zip(ra['rows'], rd['rows']):
        V *= 1.0 + float(L['g'])
        cum += row['L']
        rows.append({'t': row['t'], 'V': V, 'annual_L': row['L'], 'cum_L': cum,
                     'D_accrued': rw['A_D'], 'rate': row['rate']})
    out['L'] = {'inputs': L, 'rows': rows,
                'A': {'family_true_T': ra['family_true_T'], 'state_true_T': ra['state_true_T'],
                      'cash_demand_total': sum(r_[2] for r_ in ra['receipts'])},
                'D': {'family_true_T': rd['family_true_T'], 'state_true_T': rd['state_true_T'],
                      'settlement_true': sum(r_[2] for r_ in rd['receipts']),
                      'annual_cash_demand': 0.0 if all(r_[1].startswith('terminal') for r_ in rd['receipts']) else None}}
    M = ex['M']
    pm = dict(p); pm['V0_m'] = float(M['V0_m'])
    n_res, n_end, g = int(M['N_reset']), int(M['N_death']), float(M['g'])
    ser = [g] * n_end
    soft = float(M['soft_factor'])
    def alpha_soft(c, soft=soft, n_res=n_res):
        return soft if c['t'] == n_res else 1.0
    opts = {'shares': {'D': 1.0}}
    runs = {'soft': run_family3(pm, 1.0, alpha_soft, ser, None, vg['heir_influx'], **opts),
            'hard': run_family3(pm, 1.0, 1.0, ser, None, vg['heir_influx'], reset=[n_res], **opts),   # one voluntary reset, at N_reset
            'none': run_family3(pm, 1.0, 1.0, ser, None, vg['heir_influx'], **opts)}
    V_res = float(M['V0_m']) * (1.0 + g) ** n_res
    out['M'] = {'inputs': M, 'V_reset': V_res, 'auction_cost': float(M['auction_cost']) * V_res,
                'options': {k: {'family_true_T': r['family_true_T'], 'state_true_T': r['state_true_T'],
                                'settlements': [(t_, k_, tv, cr) for (t_, k_, tv, cr) in r['receipts']
                                                if k_ != 'tax_D']}
                            for k, r in runs.items()}}
    return out


def _headline_alphas(p: dict) -> list:
    """Declaration ratios on the HLC axis: the conventional-baseline grid (sweep + ext + extra)."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    return sorted(set(p['sweep']['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext'] + vg['conv_extra_alphas']))


def _p5_headline(p: dict, rules: list, lams: list) -> dict:
    """
    HLC core view: the WDT best response at each declaration ratio alpha.
    For each alpha the strategy slice is every strategy that deviates at exactly that ratio
    (constant (a,1) (1,a) (a,a); first_gen_only, late_deviation, correct_before_death on
    C / D / CD; voluntary_reset, pre_reset_deviation and reset_gaming on D, each with the family's own reset cycle;
    route_shift when alpha < 1; strategies that do not misdeclare, an honest reset or a Route B election, are not at any
    ratio and are left out). Best =
    max gain over that slice, so it is the max over the other strategy dimensions (target,
    family, k, route). alpha = 1 is honest (gain 0). A lower bound, like the library search.
    Emitted per (rule, lambda) so presentation never re-aggregates.
    """
    vg  = p['val_gen']
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    tol = vg['state_tol']
    out = {}
    for rule in rules:
        out[rule] = {}
        for lam in lams:
            by_a = {}
            for a in _headline_alphas(p):
                if a == 1.0:
                    by_a[str(a)] = {'gain': 0.0, 'pv_rel': 0.0, 'state_rel': 0.0,
                                    'label': 'honest', 'n_strategies': 0}
                    continue
                if a <= 0.0:    # a zero declared price: in-kind units = L / price is undefined
                    by_a[str(a)] = {'gain': None, 'pv_rel': None, 'state_rel': None,
                                    'label': 'undefined (zero declared price)', 'n_strategies': 0}
                    continue
                sl = [st for st in _strategies(p, [1.0, a]) if _direction(st) != 'none']
                ms, _ = _gains_batch(p, rule, lam, ser, sl)
                best = None
                for st, m in zip(sl, ms):
                    if best is None or m['gain'] > best['gain']:
                        best = {'gain': m['gain'], 'pv_rel': m['pv_rel'], 'state_rel': m['state_rel'],
                                'label': _label(st)}
                best['n_strategies'] = len(sl)
                by_a[str(a)] = best
            out[rule][str(lam)] = by_a
    return out


def _p5_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P5 checks: strategy functions, the rule switches, and the caps across all of them."""
    checks, info = {}, {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    vg  = p['val_gen']
    g, T, G = p['g_real'], vg['T'], vg['G']
    ser = [g] * T
    rho = p['rho']
    lam = vg['lambda_base']
    d5  = _p3_new_diag()

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            d5[key] = max(d5[key], d[key])
        for key in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units'):
            d5[key] = min(d5[key], d[key])
        if abs(sum(run['ledger'].bal.values())) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, run['family_true_T']):
            raise AssertionError('P5 ledger does not balance')

    # rule sets exercised by the checks: the ablation chain up to the simple universal candidate
    rules_chk = ('units', 'units_and_value', 'units_and_value/allow/on', 'units_and_value/reset/on')

    # a strategy function that returns a constant is the constant
    worst = 0.0
    for rule in rules_chk:
        o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam)
        for aC, aD in ((0.5, 1.0), (2.0, 0.5), (5.0, 2.0)):
            r0 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', **o)
            r1 = run_family3(p, lambda c, a=aC: a, lambda c, a=aD: a, ser, G, 'delta', **o)
            worst = max(worst, abs(r1['family_true_T'] - r0['family_true_T']))
    check('strategy_function_equals_constant', worst < 1e-12, f'max|diff|={worst:.2e}')

    # honest strategies have zero gain under every rule
    worst = 0.0
    for rule in rules_chk:
        o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam)
        m = family3_pair(p, lambda c: 1.0, lambda c: 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, **o)
        worst = max(worst, abs(m['gain']), abs(m['state_rel'] or 0.0), abs(m['pv_rel'] or 0.0))
    check('honest_strategy_zero_gain_all_rules', worst < 1e-12, f'max={worst:.2e}')

    # one life: first-generation-only is the constant
    o = _p5_opts(p, 'units', lam)
    worst = 0.0
    for a in (0.5, 2.0):
        r0 = run_family3(p, a, a, ser, None, 'delta', **o)
        r1 = run_family3(p, lambda c, a=a: a if c['gen'] == 0 else 1.0,
                         lambda c, a=a: a if c['gen'] == 0 else 1.0, ser, None, 'delta', **o)
        worst = max(worst, abs(r1['family_true_T'] - r0['family_true_T']))
    check('first_gen_only_equals_constant_for_one_life', worst < 1e-12, f'max|diff|={worst:.2e}')

    # the value cap: Route C refunds never exceed the true value paid; the units cap alone does
    net_units = net_value = 0.0
    for st in _strategies(p)[::5]:                      # every fifth library strategy, with its own reset / election / migration
        for cap in _C_CAP:
            oc = _p5_opts(p, cap, 0.0)
            r = run_family3(p, st['aC'], st['aD'], ser, G, 'delta', **{**oc, **_own(st, oc['shares'])})
            absorb(r)
            tot = sum(v_ for (_, k_, v_, _c) in r['receipts'] if k_.endswith('_C') or k_.endswith('_Cv'))
            if cap == 'units':
                net_units = min(net_units, tot)
            else:
                net_value = min(net_value, tot)
                if r['diag']['min_EC'] < -1e-9:
                    raise AssertionError(f"VALIDATION FAILED: min_EC {r['diag']['min_EC']}")
    info['most_negative_net_route_C_receipt'] = {'units': net_units, 'units_and_value': net_value}
    check('value_cap_stops_route_C_refunding_more_than_was_paid', net_value > -1e-9,
          f'units cap alone: most negative net C receipt £{net_units:,.0f}m; with value cap: £{net_value:.2e}m')
    o_u = _p5_opts(p, 'units', 0.0)
    r_a = run_family3(p, 2.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **o_u)
    r_b = run_family3(p, 2.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **{k_: v_ for k_, v_ in o_u.items() if k_ != 'c_cap'})
    check('default_cap_is_units', abs(r_a['family_true_T'] - r_b['family_true_T']) < 1e-12)

    # caps and conservation across rules, strategies, lambda
    # (the whole library as batches: the kernel's own invariants, every line)
    n_runs = 0
    lib = _strategies(p)
    for rule in rules_chk + ('units/reset/off',):
        for lam_ in (0.0, lam, 1.0):
            o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam_)
            B = run_batch(p, [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [_line(st, o['shares']) for st in lib], ser, G, 'delta', **o)
            for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
                d5[key] = max(d5[key], B['diag'][key])
            for key in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units'):
                d5[key] = min(d5[key], B['diag'][key])
            n_runs += len(lib) + 1
    check('p5_caps_hold_all_rules_and_strategies',
          d5['min_E_cash'] > -1e-9 and d5['min_A_D'] > -1e-12 and d5['min_u_out'] > -1e-12
          and d5['min_state_units'] > -1e-12 and d5['uout_err'] < 1e-12,
          f"{n_runs} runs; min u_out={d5['min_u_out']:.2e}")
    # batch (line axis) = single run (ledger), for a spread of the library
    worst = 0.0
    for rule, lam_ in (('units', 0.0), (_CANDIDATE_RULE, lam)):
        o = _p5_opts(p, rule, lam_)
        pick = lib[::9]
        B = run_batch(p, [{'aC': 1.0, 'aD': 1.0}] + [_line(st, o['shares']) for st in pick], ser, G, 'delta',
                      rhos=[rho], **o)
        for i, st in enumerate(pick, start=1):
            r = run_family3(p, st['aC'], st['aD'], ser, G, 'delta', **{**o, **_own(st, o['shares'])})
            worst = max(worst, abs(r['family_true_T'] - B['family_true_T'][i]) / r['family_true_T'],
                        abs(r['state_true_T'] - B['state_true_T'][i]) / r['state_true_T'],
                        abs(pv_true(r, rho) - B['pv'][rho][i]) / max(1.0, abs(pv_true(r, rho))))
    check('batch_engine_equals_ledger_run', worst < 1e-12, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')
    bad = 0
    for kw in ({'reset_interval': 10}, {'death_waiver': 5}):
        try:
            run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **kw)
        except TypeError:
            bad += 1
    check('retired_clock_switches_are_rejected', bad == 2, f'{bad} of 2 raised')
    # the corrective-auction switches (verify_down, Route D hazard)
    h_ref = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **_p5_opts(p, 'units_and_value/allow/off', lam))
    worst = 0.0
    for vd in ('allow', 'reset'):
        for da in ('off', 'on'):
            h_ = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta',
                             **_p5_opts(p, f'units_and_value/{vd}/{da}', lam))
            worst = max(worst, abs(h_['family_true_T'] - h_ref['family_true_T']) / h_ref['family_true_T'])
    check('auction_switches_inert_for_honest_family', worst < 1e-12, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')
    o_allow = _p5_opts(p, 'units_and_value/allow/on', lam)
    o_reset = _p5_opts(p, 'units_and_value/reset/on', lam)
    g_allow = family3_pair(p, 10.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=h_ref, **o_allow)['gain']
    g_reset = family3_pair(p, 10.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=h_ref, **o_reset)['gain']
    info['alpha_C_10_gain_allow_vs_reset'] = {'allow': g_allow, 'reset': g_reset}
    check('reset_rule_removes_overstatement_gain', g_reset < 0.005 and g_reset <= g_allow + 1e-12,   # was g_allow > 3% (tuned to nominal growth)
          f'allow {g_allow:+.2%}; reset {g_reset:+.2%}')
    h_a = run_family3(p, 3.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **o_reset)
    o_off = dict(o_reset, verify_hazard_D=0.0)
    h_b = run_family3(p, 3.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **o_off)
    check('route_D_auction_inert_when_alpha_D_is_1',
          abs(h_a['family_true_T'] - h_b['family_true_T']) < 1e-9 * h_b['family_true_T'],
          f"rel diff={abs(h_a['family_true_T'] - h_b['family_true_T']) / h_b['family_true_T']:.2e}")
    bad = 0
    for kw in ({'c_cap': 'x'}, {'verify_down': 'x'}, {'verify_hazard_D': 1.5}, {'verify_hazard': 2.0}):
        try:
            run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **kw)
        except ValueError:
            bad += 1
    check('invalid_switch_values_raise', bad == 4, f'{bad} of 4 raised')
    # conventional reference system: honest burden matches the WDT, and the gain is monotone in
    # understatement (declaring less always pays more, with no interior optimum)
    alphas_c = sorted(set(p['sweep']['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext'] + vg['conv_extra_alphas']))
    conv = _p5_conventional(p, alphas_c)
    h_w = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **_p5_opts(p, _CANDIDATE_RULE, 0.0))
    diag = [conv['diag_alpha'][str(a)] for a in alphas_c]
    check('conventional_baseline_matches_wdt_honest_burden',
          abs(conv['honest_TW'] - h_w['family_true_T']) < 1e-6 * h_w['family_true_T'],
          f"flat rate {conv['rate']:.3%}; TW {conv['honest_TW']:,.1f} vs {h_w['family_true_T']:,.1f}")
    check('conventional_gain_monotone_in_understatement',
          all(diag[i + 1] < diag[i] + 1e-12 for i in range(len(diag) - 1)) and conv['best']['gain'] > 0.1,
          f"alpha {alphas_c[0]}: {diag[0]:+.1%} ... alpha {alphas_c[-1]}: {diag[-1]:+.1%}")
    check('p5_conservation', d5['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max err={d5['cons_err']:.2e}")
    check('p5_in_kind_identity', d5['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL, f"max rel err={d5['unit_err']:.2e}")
    return checks, info


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAIN
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P6 — ROUTE B LIEN / INCOME, DEATH VERIFICATION, ARCHETYPES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

_P6_MODES = ('sale', 'lien', 'income')


def _p6_lien_hand(pf: dict, g: float, T: int, r_def: float) -> tuple:
    """Independent hand recursion for a Route B-only family under the lien, flat rate, honest, no deaths.
    Declared wealth is net of the lien; the tax on a rise is tau x delta and is added to the balance, which
    accrues at r_def from the next year. Returns (LB at T, family true wealth at T, V_T)."""
    V, LBp, tau0 = pf['V0_m'], 0.0, pf['tau_0']
    for _ in range(T):
        V_prev = V
        V *= 1.0 + g
        LBa = LBp * (1.0 + r_def)
        delta = (V - LBa) - (V_prev - LBp)
        L = tau0 * delta
        if delta <= 0.0:
            raise ValueError('hand case needs a rising net wealth every year')
        LBp = LBa + L
    return LBp, V - LBp, V


def _p6_validate(p: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:
    """P6 checks: defaults inert, hand cases for the lien and income scenarios, conservation, death verification."""
    checks, info = {}, {}

    def check(name, ok, detail=''):
        checks[name] = {'ok': bool(ok), 'detail': detail}
        if not ok:
            raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: {name} {detail}')

    vg, g, rho = p['val_gen'], p['g_real'], p['rho']
    T, G = vg['T'], vg['G']
    ir = _ir(p) if vg['index_wmin'] else 0.0
    ser = [g] * T
    fp = _flat(p)
    rb = p.get('route_b') or {}
    r_def = rb.get('r_def', 0.025)
    base = dict(consumption=vg['consumption'], index_rate=ir, shares=dict(vg['route_shares']))
    d6 = _p3_new_diag()

    def absorb(run):
        d = run['diag']
        for key in ('cons_err', 'unit_err', 'uout_err'):
            d6[key] = max(d6[key], d[key])
        for key in ('min_E_cash', 'min_A_D', 'min_u_out', 'min_state_units'):
            d6[key] = min(d6[key], d[key])
        led = run['ledger']
        if abs(sum(led.bal.values())) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, run['family_true_T']):
            raise AssertionError('P6 ledger does not balance')
        if abs(led.bal['income'] + led.bal['state_cash']) > 1e-9 * max(1.0, run['family_true_T']):
            raise AssertionError('P6 income account does not equal state cash')

    # 1. the new switches at their defaults reproduce the earlier engine exactly
    worst = 0.0
    for aC, aD in ((1.0, 1.0), (0.5, 0.5), (2.0, 0.5)):
        r0 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', **base)
        r1 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', route_b='sale', r_def=r_def, income_ratio=0.0,
                         income_cap=1.0, death_verify=False, **base)
        absorb(r1)
        worst = max(worst, abs(r1['family_true_T'] - r0['family_true_T']) + abs(r1['state_true_T'] - r0['state_true_T']))
    check('p6_defaults_reproduce_sale_engine', worst < 1e-12, f'max diff={worst:.2e}')

    # 2. lien hand case: Route B only, flat rate, honest, no deaths
    Th = 30
    sh_b = dict(shares={'B': 1.0}, consumption=0.0, index_rate=0.0)
    worst = 0.0
    for rd in (0.0, 0.025, 0.06):
        run = run_family3(fp, 1.0, 1.0, [g] * Th, None, 'delta', route_b='lien', r_def=rd, **sh_b)
        absorb(run)
        LB, fam, V_T = _p6_lien_hand(fp, g, Th, rd)
        worst = max(worst, abs(run['family_true_T'] - fam) / V_T, abs(run['state_true_T'] - LB) / V_T)
        info[f'lien_hand_LB_T_r{rd}'] = LB
    check('p6_lien_matches_hand_recursion', worst < 1e-9, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')

    # 3. income hand case: ample income pays every tax; no units move; the state holds cash
    rich = run_family3(fp, 1.0, 1.0, [g] * Th, None, 'delta', route_b='income', income_ratio=1e6,
                       income_cap=1.0, **sh_b)
    absorb(rich)
    V, tax = fp['V0_m'], 0.0
    for _ in range(Th):
        V_prev = V
        V *= 1.0 + g
        tax += fp['tau_0'] * (V - V_prev)
    cash = rich['ledger'].bal['state_cash']
    check('p6_income_hand_case_state_cash_equals_sum_of_tax',
          abs(cash - tax) < 1e-9 * V and abs(rich['family_true_T'] - V) < 1e-9 * V and rich['unpaid_B'] == 0.0
          and abs(rich['income_paid'] - cash) < 1e-12,
          f'state cash {cash:.4f} vs hand {tax:.4f}; family {rich["family_true_T"]:.4f} vs V_T {V:.4f}')

    # 4. income that is too small: the shortfall is sold, and the value moved equals the tax assessed
    short = run_family3(fp, 1.0, 1.0, [g] * Th, None, 'delta', route_b='income', income_ratio=0.002,
                        income_cap=1.0, **sh_b)
    absorb(short)
    credited = sum(c_ for (_, _k, _v, c_) in short['receipts'])
    assessed = sum(x_['L'] for x_ in short['rows'] if 'L' in x_)
    check('p6_income_shortfall_is_sold_and_conserved',
          0.0 < short['income_paid'] < tax and short['f_T']['B'] < 1.0
          and abs(credited - assessed) < 1e-9 * V and short['diag']['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL,
          f"income paid {short['income_paid']:.3f}; units kept {short['f_T']['B']:.4f}; "
          f"credited receipts {credited:.4f} vs assessed {assessed:.4f}")

    # 5. zero income = sale mode exactly
    worst = 0.0
    for aC, aD in ((1.0, 1.0), (0.5, 0.5)):
        r0 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', route_b='sale', **base)
        r1 = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', route_b='income', income_ratio=0.0, **base)
        absorb(r1)
        worst = max(worst, abs(r1['family_true_T'] - r0['family_true_T']) + abs(r1['state_true_T'] - r0['state_true_T']))
    check('p6_zero_income_equals_sale', worst < 1e-12, f'max diff={worst:.2e}')

    # 6. a higher deferral rate leaves the family poorer (hand case and the family mix with deaths)
    lo = run_family3(fp, 1.0, 1.0, [g] * Th, None, 'delta', route_b='lien', r_def=0.01, **sh_b)['family_true_T']
    hi = run_family3(fp, 1.0, 1.0, [g] * Th, None, 'delta', route_b='lien', r_def=0.08, **sh_b)['family_true_T']
    mix = dict(base, shares={'A': 0.3, 'B': 0.5, 'C': 0.1, 'D': 0.1})
    lo2 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', route_b='lien', r_def=0.01, **mix)['family_true_T']
    hi2 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', route_b='lien', r_def=0.08, **mix)['family_true_T']
    check('p6_lien_family_wealth_falls_with_deferral_rate', hi < lo and hi2 < lo2,
          f'hand {lo:.2f} -> {hi:.2f}; mix {lo2:.2f} -> {hi2:.2f}')

    # 7. conservation, ledger balance and caps over modes x strategies x shares, with deaths
    n_runs = 0
    for mode in _P6_MODES:
        for shares in (dict(base['shares']), {'A': 0.2, 'B': 0.5, 'C': 0.2, 'D': 0.1}):
            for ratio in ((0.0,) if mode != 'income' else (0.0, 0.01, 0.2)):
                for aC, aD in ((1.0, 1.0), (0.5, 0.5), (2.0, 0.5), (0.1, 2.0)):
                    for dv in (False, True):
                        run = run_family3(p, aC, aD, ser, G, 'delta', route_b=mode, r_def=r_def,
                                          income_ratio=ratio, death_verify=dv, **dict(base, shares=shares))
                        absorb(run)
                        n_runs += 1
    check('p6_conservation_and_caps_all_modes',
          d6['cons_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL and d6['unit_err'] < CONSERVE_TOL and d6['min_E_cash'] > -1e-9
          and d6['min_A_D'] > -1e-12 and d6['min_u_out'] > -1e-12 and d6['min_state_units'] > -1e-12
          and d6['uout_err'] < 1e-12, f"{n_runs} runs; cons {d6['cons_err']:.1e}, unit {d6['unit_err']:.1e}")

    # 8. death verification is inert for the honest family
    worst = 0.0
    for lam in (0.0, vg['lambda_base']):
        a0 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', verify_hazard=lam, **base)
        a1 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', verify_hazard=lam, death_verify=True, **base)
        absorb(a1)
        worst = max(worst, abs(a1['family_true_T'] - a0['family_true_T']) / a0['family_true_T'],
                    abs(a1['state_true_T'] - a0['state_true_T']) / a0['state_true_T'])
    check('p6_death_verification_inert_for_honest_family', worst < 1e-9, f'max rel diff={worst:.2e}')

    # 9. death verification takes the understatement gain away (C-heavy mix, alpha_C = 0.5)
    heavy = dict(base, shares={'A': 0.5, 'C': 0.5})
    gains = {}
    for dv in (False, True):
        h = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', death_verify=dv, **heavy)
        gains[dv] = family3_pair(p, 0.5, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', rho, honest=h, death_verify=dv, **heavy)['gain']
    info['death_verify_gain_alpha_C_0.5'] = {'off': gains[False], 'on': gains[True]}
    check('p6_death_verification_erodes_understatement_gain', gains[True] < gains[False] - 1e-9,
          f'{gains[False]:+.3%} without, {gains[True]:+.3%} with')

    # 10. invalid switches raise
    bad = 0
    for kw in ({'route_b': 'x'}, {'income_cap': 1.5}, {'income_ratio': -0.1}, {'r_def': -1.5}):
        try:
            run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, ser, G, 'delta', **kw)
        except ValueError:
            bad += 1
    check('p6_invalid_switch_values_raise', bad == 4, f'{bad} of 4 raised')
    return checks, info


def _p6_breakeven_spread(pm: dict, ser: list, target_pv: float, o: dict) -> float | None:
    """Deferral spread over the sovereign real rate at which the PV of the state's receipts under the lien equals
    the sale-mode PV (the state is indifferent to the deferral). Bisection on [-4%, +30%]; None if not bracketed."""
    vg, rb = pm['val_gen'], pm['route_b']

    def f(s):
        q = dict(pm, route_b=dict(rb, payment_mode='lien', r_def=rb['sovereign_real_rate'] + s))
        run = run_family3(q, 1.0, 1.0, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **dict(o, **_phase2_opts(q)))
        return pv_true(run, pm['rho']) - target_pv
    lo, hi = -0.04, 0.30
    flo, fhi = f(lo), f(hi)
    if flo * fhi > 0.0:
        return None
    for _ in range(60):
        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)
        fm = f(mid)
        if flo * fm <= 0.0:
            hi = mid
        else:
            lo, flo = mid, fm
    return 0.5 * (lo + hi)


def _p6_archetypes(p: dict) -> dict:
    """The five archetypes of plan section 4 through the family engine: honest outcomes under sale, lien and
    income, the best-response gain under the candidate rule (lambda 0 and the base lambda), and the breakeven
    deferral spread. Empty if the parameter file has no [archetypes] / [route_b] block."""
    arch, rb = p.get('archetypes'), p.get('route_b')
    if not arch or not rb:
        return {}
    vg = p['val_gen']
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    strategies = _strategies(p)
    lams = (0.0, vg['lambda_base'])
    out = {}
    for name, a in arch.items():
        pa = dict(p, V0_m=a['V0_m'], val_gen=dict(vg, route_shares=dict(a['shares'])), archetype=name)
        row = {'label': a['label'], 'V0_m': a['V0_m'], 'shares': dict(a['shares']),
               'income_ratio': _phase2_opts(pa).get('income_ratio', 0.0), 'modes': {}}
        for mode in _P6_MODES:
            pm = dict(pa, route_b=dict(rb, payment_mode=mode))
            o = _p5_opts(pm, _CANDIDATE_RULE, 0.0)
            h = run_family3(pm, 1.0, 1.0, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **o)
            cell = {'TW': h['family_true_T'], 'PV': pv_true(h, p['rho']), 'state_true_T': h['state_true_T'],
                    'income_paid': h['income_paid'], 'unpaid_B': h['unpaid_B'], 'best': {}}
            for lam in lams:
                s = _p5_search(pm, _CANDIDATE_RULE, lam, strategies)
                cell['best'][str(lam)] = {'gain': s['best']['gain'], 'label': s['best']['label'],
                                          'BRG': s['BRG_pass'], 'SPT': s['SPT_pass'], 'SST': s['SST_pass']}
            row['modes'][mode] = cell
        pm = dict(pa, route_b=dict(rb, payment_mode='lien'))
        row['breakeven_spread'] = _p6_breakeven_spread(pm, ser, row['modes']['sale']['PV'],
                                                       _p5_opts(pm, _CANDIDATE_RULE, 0.0))
        out[name] = row
    return out


def _p6_print(arch: dict):
    if not arch:
        print('  (no [archetypes] / [route_b] in the parameter file: archetype runs skipped)')
        return
    for name, r_ in arch.items():
        sh = ' '.join(f'{k}{v:.0%}' for k, v in r_['shares'].items())
        be = r_['breakeven_spread']
        print(f"  {name} (V0 £{r_['V0_m']:g}m; {sh}; income/wealth {r_['income_ratio']:.1%}); "
              f"breakeven deferral spread {'not bracketed in [-4%, +30%]' if be is None else format(be, '+.2%')} (state receipts PV equal to sale)")
        for mode, c in r_['modes'].items():
            b0, b1 = c['best']['0.0'], list(c['best'].values())[-1]
            print(f"    {mode:<7} honest TW £{c['TW']:,.1f}m, state PV £{c['PV']:,.1f}m, income paid £{c['income_paid']:,.1f}m, "
                  f"unpaid B £{c['unpaid_B']:,.2f}m; best response {b0['gain']:+.1%} (lambda 0), {b1['gain']:+.1%} (base lambda)")


def _geo_mean(xs: list) -> float:
    return math.exp(sum(math.log1p(x) for x in xs) / len(xs)) - 1.0


def _p7_summary(rows: list, key: str) -> dict:
    """Share of windows passing BRG / SST and the spread of the best-response gain, full loop and contiguous-only."""
    out = {}
    for name, keep in (('full_loop', lambda r: True), ('contiguous', lambda r: r['contiguous'])):
        cells = [r['cells'][key] for r in rows if keep(r)]
        if not cells:
            out[name] = None
            continue
        gains = sorted(c['gain'] for c in cells)
        out[name] = {'windows': len(cells),
                     'BRG_pass_share': sum(1 for c in cells if c['BRG']) / len(cells),
                     'SST_pass_share': sum(1 for c in cells if c['SST']) / len(cells),
                     'gain_max': gains[-1], 'gain_median': gains[len(gains) // 2], 'gain_min': gains[0]}
    return out


def _p7_replay(p: dict, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """
    D1a / D1b. The headline rule sets x lambda {0, lambda_base} on the REAL JST capital-return path of each loop window of
    [val_gen] replay_countries (wdt_jst.loop_windows, wrap = True; every start_stride-th start). T = [val_gen] T. The strategy
    library runs once per window. Windows that repeat years are flagged (`repeat`), not dropped; `contiguous` marks windows that
    cross no seam, summarised separately. index_rate stays the constant of the basis. Returns {} content 'skipped' when replay_stride = 0.
    """
    vg = p['val_gen']
    stride = int(vg.get('replay_stride', 0))
    if stride <= 0 or not vg.get('replay_countries'):
        print('  (JST replay skipped: replay_stride = 0 or no replay_countries)')
        return {'skipped': True}
    rp = p['rates']
    J = load_jst(rp['jst_path'])
    T = vg['T']
    rules = vg['headline_rules']
    lams = [0.0, vg['lambda_base']]
    out = {'T': T, 'stride': stride, 'rules': rules, 'lambda_vals': lams,
           'note': 'real JST capital return path (CPI-deflated) per loop window; constant index_rate; wrap = True, repeats flagged',
           'countries': {}}
    for iso in vg['replay_countries']:
        r = real_return_series(J, iso)
        years = sorted(r)
        wins = loop_windows(years, T, wrap=True)[::stride]
        rows = []
        for w in wins:
            ser = [r[y] for y in w['years']]
            cells = {}
            for rule in rules:
                for lam in lams:
                    s = _p5_search(p, rule, lam, strategies, ser=ser)
                    cells[f'{rule}|{lam}'] = {'gain': s['best']['gain'], 'label': s['best']['label'], 'BRG': s['BRG_pass'],
                                              'SST': s['SST_pass'], 'SPT': s['SPT_pass'], 'n_conflict': s['n_conflict']}
            rows.append({'start': w['start'], 'wraps': w['wraps'], 'repeat': w['repeat'], 'contiguous': w['contiguous'],
                         'g_geo': _geo_mean(ser), 'cells': cells})
        summ = {k: _p7_summary(rows, k) for k in rows[0]['cells']} if rows else {}
        out['countries'][iso] = {'usable_years': len(years), 'windows': len(rows),
                                 'repeat_windows': sum(1 for x in rows if x['repeat']), 'rows': rows, 'summary': summ}
        print(f"  replay {iso}: {len(years)} usable years, {len(rows)} windows (stride {stride}), "
              f"{sum(1 for x in rows if x['contiguous'])} contiguous, {sum(1 for x in rows if x['repeat'])} with repeats")
        for k, sm in summ.items():
            for nm in ('full_loop', 'contiguous'):
                c = sm[nm]
                if c:
                    print(f"    {k:<34} {nm:<9} n={c['windows']:>3} BRG pass {c['BRG_pass_share']:.0%} SST pass {c['SST_pass_share']:.0%} "
                          f"best gain median {c['gain_median']:+.2%} max {c['gain_max']:+.2%}")
    return out


def _p3_lambda_grid(p: dict, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """lambda_C x lambda_D: the two verification hazards varied INDEPENDENTLY (D6), under the candidate rule set (the Route D
    corrective auction is on there; under the base rule lambda_D is inert). Best response, verdicts and the strategy per cell."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    sweep = (p.get('verification') or {}).get('lambda_sweep') or [0.0, vg['lambda_base']]
    out = {'lambda_C': list(sweep), 'lambda_D': list(sweep), 'rule': _CANDIDATE_RULE, 'cells': {},
           'note': 'lambda_C (Route C verification) and lambda_D (Route D corrective auction) varied independently; best response over the strategy library'}
    for lc in sweep:
        for ld in sweep:
            s = _p5_search(p, _CANDIDATE_RULE, lc, strategies, lam_D=ld)
            out['cells'][f'{lc}|{ld}'] = {'gain': s['best']['gain'], 'label': s['best']['label'], 'BRG': s['BRG_pass'],
                                          'SST': s['SST_pass'], 'SPT': s['SPT_pass'], 'n_conflict': s['n_conflict']}
    return out


def _v0_sweep(p: dict, strategies: list) -> dict:
    """The V0 sweep across the RATES revenue bands ([rates.run].revenue_bands_gbp_m, launch wealth in £m): headline rule sets x lambda
    {0, lambda_base}. Route shares stay at the [val_gen] baseline mix (the archetype mixture by band is RATES' job). Per cell: the best
    response and verdicts, the honest family's terminal wealth and its tax drag against a no-tax run."""
    vg = p['val_gen']
    bands = list(p['rates']['run']['revenue_bands_gbp_m'])
    lams = [0.0, vg['lambda_base']]
    out = {'bands': bands, 'rules': list(vg['headline_rules']), 'lambda_vals': lams, 'cells': {},
           'note': 'V0 = RATES revenue band (£m); route shares at the baseline mix; drag = 1 - honest terminal wealth / no-tax terminal wealth'}
    ser = [p['g_real']] * vg['T']
    for b in bands:
        pb = dict(p, V0_m=float(b))
        tw_free = _p5_no_tax_tw(pb)
        for rule in vg['headline_rules']:
            for lam in lams:
                s = _p5_search(pb, rule, lam, strategies)
                h = run_family3(pb, 1.0, 1.0, ser, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **_p5_opts(pb, rule, lam))
                out['cells'][f'{b}|{rule}|{lam}'] = {
                    'gain': s['best']['gain'], 'label': s['best']['label'], 'BRG': s['BRG_pass'], 'SST': s['SST_pass'],
                    'SPT': s['SPT_pass'], 'n_conflict': s['n_conflict'], 'honest_TW': h['family_true_T'],
                    'drag': 1.0 - h['family_true_T'] / tw_free}
    return out


def _rates_burdens(p: dict) -> dict:
    """
    HLC burdens (D1d) from the TOML-held calibration [val_gen.hlc]; valgen reads no RATES output.
    average = wealth-weighted annual WDT / wealth over net payers; top = top 0.1%.  Regenerate with test/print_hlc_calibration.py.
    Returns {'ok': False, 'reason': ...} when the block is absent or still a PLACEHOLDER.
    """
    h = p['val_gen'].get('hlc')
    if not h:
        return {'ok': False, 'reason': '[val_gen.hlc] absent from the TOML'}
    if h['placeholder']:
        return {'ok': False, 'reason': '[val_gen.hlc] is a PLACEHOLDER; run RATES, then test/print_hlc_calibration.py --write'}
    return {'ok': True, 'scenario': h['source_scenario'], 'stamp': h['stamp'], 'average': h['average_stock_rate'],
            'top': h['top_stock_rate'], 'by_band': None, 'wealth_share': None}


def _hlc_pair(p: dict) -> dict:
    """HLC pair: the conventional self-declared tax at the burden of the average payer and of the top payer (RATES), against the WDT.
    Skipped, with the reason, while [val_gen.hlc] is absent or a PLACEHOLDER. Burden = annual rate on declared value, equal to the stock rate."""
    b = _rates_burdens(p)
    if not b['ok']:
        print(f"  (HLC pair skipped: {b['reason']})")
        return {'skipped': True, 'reason': b['reason']}
    vg = p['val_gen']
    alphas = _headline_alphas(p)
    out = {'skipped': False, 'source': {'scenario': b['scenario'], 'stamp': b['stamp'], 'by_band': b['by_band'], 'wealth_share': b['wealth_share'],
                                        'definition': 'average = net payers, wealth-weighted; top = top 0.1% (D1d); from [val_gen.hlc]'},
           'burdens': {}}
    for label, rate in (('average', b['average']), ('top', b['top'])):
        out['burdens'][label] = _p5_conventional(p, alphas, rate=rate)
    return out


_RETIRED_KEYS = ('reset_interval', 'death_waiver')   # still parsed by wdt_core.load_params until D11; no reader here and not stamped


def _clean(obj):
    """Plain JSON types; nan/inf -> None."""
    if isinstance(obj, dict):
        return {str(k): _clean(v) for k, v in obj.items()}
    if isinstance(obj, (list, tuple)):
        return [_clean(v) for v in obj]
    if isinstance(obj, float) and not math.isfinite(obj):
        return None
    return obj


def _fmt(v):
    return f'{v:+7.1%}' if v is not None else '    n/a'


def main(dry_run: bool = False):
    print('valgen_core.py — VAL generational model, P1 / P2 / P2b / P3 / P4 / P5')
    print('=' * 50)
    p = with_val_basis(with_rate_scenario(load_params()))      # rate design from [val_gen] rate_scenario
    N, g = p['N_val'], p['g_real']
    vg = p['val_gen']
    print(f"Parameters: k={p['k']}, tau_0={p['tau_0']}, tau_m={p['tau_m']}, "
          f"W_min=£{p['W_min']}m, N_val={N}, g={g:.4f}")
    sw = p['sweep']
    print(f"Grids: {len(sw['alpha_vals'])} alpha, {len(sw['g_vals'])} g, "
          f"{len(sw['n_actual_vals'])} N, {len(vg['consumption_vals'])} consumption")
    if dry_run:
        print('Dry run — skipping simulations.')
        return

    print('\n[1/9] Bridge to legacy run_pair / run_sim_hist...')
    bridge = _bridge(p)
    life = _life_results(p)
    life['route_d_examples'] = _route_d_examples(p)
    print(f"  LIFE: {len(life['grid'])} grid cells, {len(life['by_n'])} N cells, {len(life['by_rho'])} rho cells, "
          f"examples {sorted(life['examples'])}")
    print(f"  {bridge['cells_constant_g']} constant-g cells x {len(sw['alpha_vals'])} alpha, "
          f"{bridge['cells_historical']} historical runs")

    print('[2/9] Validating P1...')
    validation = _validate(p, bridge)
    for name, c in validation['checks'].items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")

    print('[3/9] P1 reference decomposition (plan §1), alpha in example_alphas...')
    series = [g] * N
    examples = {}
    for a in p['val_gen']['example_alphas']:
        r = run_life(p, a, series, g)
        examples[str(a)] = {'decomposition': _decomp(r), 'rows': r['rows']}
        d = _decomp(r)
        print(f"  alpha={a}: hold {d['holding_payments_true']:.1f} / sell {d['sell_year_cash']:+.1f} / "
              f"settle {d['post_sale_settlement']:+.1f} / TW pre {d['TW_before_settlement']:.1f} / "
              f"TW settled {d['TW_settled']:.1f}")
    pairs = {str(a): pair(p, a, series, g, p['rho']) for a in sw['alpha_vals']}

    print('[4/9] P2 validation (single life, plan §1 benchmark, heirs)...')
    p2_checks, p2_data = _p2_validate(p)
    for name, c in p2_checks.items():
        print(f"  {'SKIP' if c.get('skipped') else 'PASS'}  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p2_checks)

    print('[5/9] P2b validation (checks 7 and 10, refund caps, rule switches)...')
    p2b_checks, p2b_info = _p2b_validate(p)
    for name, c in p2b_checks.items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p2b_checks)
    o = p2b_info['oscillation']
    print(f"  INFO  one-off delta 100: net tax {o['net_engine']:.3f}, first flows "
          f"{[round(x, 2) for x in o['first_flows']]}")
    print(f"  INFO  round trip +50% then back, flat 15%: units "
          f"ratio_mirror {p2b_info['round_trip_units']['ratio_mirror']:.5f}, "
          f"legacy {p2b_info['round_trip_units']['legacy']:.5f}")

    print('[6/9] P2b family grid: consumption x refund rule, W_min indexed...')
    fseries = [g] * vg['T']
    ir = _ir(p) if vg['index_wmin'] else 0.0
    tol = vg['state_tol']
    grid = {}
    for c in vg['consumption_vals']:
        for rule in _REFUND_RULES:
            key = f'c={c}|{rule}'
            cells = {str(a): family_pair(p, a, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'],
                                         vg['envelope_unit'], p['rho'], consumption=c,
                                         index_rate=ir, refund_rule=rule)
                     for a in sw['alpha_vals']}
            al = alignment(cells, tol)
            grid[key] = {'cells': cells, 'alignment': al,
                         'V_T_honest': cells['1.0']['V_T']}
    print(f"  T={vg['T']}, G={vg['G']}, heir={vg['heir_influx']}, envelope={vg['envelope_unit']}, "
          f"index={ir:.2%}, state_tol=±{tol:.0%}")
    for key, v in grid.items():
        print(f"  {key}: honest V_T £{v['V_T_honest']:,.0f}m; conflict at alpha="
              f"{v['alignment']['conflict']}; aligned {v['alignment']['aligned']}")
        print('    alpha : ' + ' '.join(f'{a:>7}' for a in v['cells']))
        print('    gain  : ' + ' '.join(_fmt(m['gain']) for m in v['cells'].values()))
        print('    pv_rel: ' + ' '.join(_fmt(m['pv_rel']) for m in v['cells'].values()))

    print('[7/9] P3 validation and four-route surface...')
    p3_checks, p3_info = _p3_validate(p)
    for name, c in p3_checks.items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p3_checks)
    print(f"  INFO  Route D, alpha_D = 0.5: gain with a voluntary reset every {p3_info['D_understate_gain_alpha_D_0.5']['cycle']}y "
          f"{p3_info['D_understate_gain_alpha_D_0.5']['reset']:+.2%}, never "
          f"{p3_info['D_understate_gain_alpha_D_0.5']['never']:+.2%}")

    shares = vg['route_shares']
    p3_opts = dict(consumption=vg['consumption'], index_rate=ir, shares=shares)
    honest3 = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **p3_opts)
    surface = {}
    for aC in sw['alpha_vals']:
        for aD in sw['alpha_vals']:
            surface[f'{aC}|{aD}'] = family3_pair(p, aC, aD, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'],
                                                 p['rho'], honest=honest3, **p3_opts)
    best = max((k for k in surface if k != '1.0|1.0'), key=lambda k: surface[k]['gain'])
    conflicts = [k for k, m in surface.items()
                 if not m['is_honest'] and m['gain'] > 0.0
                 and (m['pv_rel'] is None or abs(m['pv_rel']) > tol)]
    print(f"  shares {shares}; no reset clock (a reset is a strategy action); honest TW £{honest3['family_true_T']:,.0f}m")
    print(f"  max family gain {surface[best]['gain']:+.2%} at (alpha_C|alpha_D) = {best}, "
          f"pv_rel {_fmt(surface[best]['pv_rel']).strip()}")
    print(f"  BRG-gain/SPT-SST conflict cells (gain > 0 and |pv_rel| > {tol:.0%} or undefined): "
          f"{len(conflicts)} of {len(surface) - 1}")
    print('    rows alpha_C, cols alpha_D; cell = gain / pv_rel')
    for aC in sw['alpha_vals']:
        print(f'    C={aC:<4} ' + ' '.join(
            f"{surface[f'{aC}|{aD}']['gain']:+6.1%}/{_fmt(surface[f'{aC}|{aD}']['pv_rel']).strip():>6}"
            for aD in sw['alpha_vals']))

    sens = {}            # the family's own voluntary reset cycle (0 = never) x alpha_D; honest = no reset, same rules
    for r_i in [0] + _reset_cycles(vg):
        sens[str(r_i)] = {str(aD): family3_pair(p, 1.0, aD, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], p['rho'],
                                                honest=honest3, own=({'reset': r_i} if r_i else None), **p3_opts)
                          for aD in sw['alpha_vals']}
    print('  Route D understatement gain by the family\'s voluntary reset cycle (alpha_C = 1; honest never resets):')
    for r_i, row in sens.items():
        print(f'    reset {r_i:>3}y: ' + ' '.join(f"{row[str(aD)]['gain']:+6.1%}" for aD in sw['alpha_vals']))

    print('[8/9] P4 verification hazard on Route C: checks, lambda sweep...')
    p4_checks, p4_info = _p4_validate(p)
    for name, c in p4_checks.items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p4_checks)

    lam_base, thr = vg['lambda_base'], vg['verified_threshold']
    lam_sweep = {}
    for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
        o4 = dict(p3_opts, verify_hazard=lam)
        h_l = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **o4)
        row_c = {str(aC): family3_pair(p, aC, 1.0, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], p['rho'],
                                       honest=h_l, **o4) for aC in sw['alpha_vals']}
        row_d = {str(aD): family3_pair(p, 1.0, aD, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], p['rho'],
                                       honest=h_l, **o4) for aD in sw['alpha_vals']}
        both = {f'{aC}|{aD}': family3_pair(p, aC, aD, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], p['rho'],
                                           honest=h_l, **o4)
                for aC in sw['alpha_vals'] for aD in sw['alpha_vals']}
        best_l = max((k for k in both if k != '1.0|1.0'), key=lambda k: both[k]['gain'])
        conf_l = [k for k, m in both.items() if not m['is_honest'] and m['gain'] > 0.0
                  and (m['pv_rel'] is None or abs(m['pv_rel']) > tol)]
        conf_s = [k for k, m in both.items() if not m['is_honest'] and m['gain'] > 0.0
                  and (m['state_rel'] is None or abs(m['state_rel']) > tol)]
        vs = [x['verified_share'] for x in h_l['rows'] if 'verified_share' in x]
        lam_sweep[str(lam)] = {
            'TW_honest': h_l['family_true_T'], 'by_alpha_C': row_c, 'by_alpha_D': row_d,
            'surface': both, 'max_gain': both[best_l]['gain'], 'max_gain_at': best_l,
            'conflict_cells': conf_l, 'conflict_cells_stake': conf_s,
            'year_verified_share_ge_threshold': _first_year_at(vs, thr) if lam > 0.0 else None,
            'verified_share_by_year': vs,
        }
    print(f"  baseline lambda {lam_base:.0%} (placeholder, no empirical anchor), threshold {thr:.0%}")
    print('  lambda  | yr to ' + f'{thr:.0%}' + ' | max gain (at C|D) | conflicts PV / stake | gain at alpha_C = ' +
          ' '.join(f'{a:>5}' for a in sw['alpha_vals']))
    for lam, v_ in lam_sweep.items():
        yrs = v_['year_verified_share_ge_threshold']
        print(f"  {float(lam):>6.0%}  | {('-' if yrs is None else yrs):>8} | "
              f"{v_['max_gain']:+6.2%} at {v_['max_gain_at']:<9} | {len(v_['conflict_cells']):>3} / "
              f"{len(v_['conflict_cells_stake']):<3} of 80 | " +
              ' '.join(f"{v_['by_alpha_C'][str(a)]['gain']:+5.1%}" for a in sw['alpha_vals']))
    print('  pv_rel at alpha_C =                                         ' +
          ' '.join(f'{a:>5}' for a in sw['alpha_vals']))
    for lam, v_ in lam_sweep.items():
        print(f"  {float(lam):>6.0%}  (alpha_D = 1)                                " +
              ' '.join(_fmt(v_['by_alpha_C'][str(a)]['pv_rel']).strip().rjust(5)
                       for a in sw['alpha_vals']))

    # sensitivity: C share across the BEHAV range (A absorbs the difference) and alpha_C beyond 2
    c_sens = {}
    a_grid = sorted(set(sw['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext']))
    for cs in vg['c_share_sens']:
        sh = dict(shares)
        sh['A'] = shares['A'] - (cs - shares['C'])
        sh['C'] = cs
        for lam in (0.0, lam_base):
            o4 = dict(p3_opts, shares=sh, verify_hazard=lam)
            h_c = run_family3(p, 1.0, 1.0, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], **o4)
            c_sens[f'C={cs}|lambda={lam}'] = {
                str(a): family3_pair(p, a, 1.0, fseries, vg['G'], vg['heir_influx'], p['rho'],
                                     honest=h_c, **o4) for a in a_grid}
    print(f"  Route C share sensitivity (alpha_D = 1), lambda = {lam_base:.0%}: "
          f"gain / state terminal stake vs honest")
    print('    C share  alpha_C: ' + ' '.join(f'{a:>14}' for a in (1.5, 2.0, 5.0, 10.0)))
    for cs in vg['c_share_sens']:
        row = c_sens[f'C={cs}|lambda={lam_base}']
        print(f'    {cs:>6.0%}           ' + ' '.join(
            f"{row[str(a)]['gain']:+6.1%}/{row[str(a)]['state_rel']:+6.1%}" for a in (1.5, 2.0, 5.0, 10.0)))

    print("  C-heavy stress (A 50 / C 50), alpha_C = 0.5, gain by lambda: " +
          ', '.join(f'{x:.0%}: {v_:+.2%}' for x, v_ in
                    sorted(p4_info['C_heavy_gain_by_lambda_alpha_C_0.5'].items())))

    print('[9/9] P5 strategy search, refund-rule levers, BRG/HSC/SPT/SST verdicts...')
    p5_checks, p5_info = _p5_validate(p)
    for name, c in p5_checks.items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p5_checks)

    print('[9b] P6 Route B lien / income, death verification, archetypes...')
    p6_checks, p6_info = _p6_validate(p)
    for name, c in p6_checks.items():
        print(f"  PASS  {name} {c['detail']}")
    validation['checks'].update(p6_checks)
    p6_arch = _p6_archetypes(p)
    _p6_print(p6_arch)
    p6_out = {'checks': p6_checks, 'info': p6_info, 'archetypes': p6_arch}

    strategies = _strategies(p)
    rules = [f'{cap}/{vd}/{da}' for cap in vg['c_cap_rules']
             for vd in vg['verify_down_rules'] for da in vg['d_auction_rules']]
    g2_full = {rule: _honest_shock_cost(p, rule) for rule in rules}
    g2 = {rule: v[0] for rule, v in g2_full.items()}
    search = {}
    for rule in rules:
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            search[f'{rule}|{lam}'] = _p5_search(p, rule, lam, strategies)
    print(f"  {len(strategies)} strategies x {len(rules)} rule sets x {len(vg['lambda_vals'])} lambda "
          f"= {len(strategies) * len(rules) * len(vg['lambda_vals'])} runs")
    print(f"  thresholds (placeholders in TOML): BRG best-response gain <= {vg['brg_tol']:.0%}; "
          f"SPT |PV| and SST |stake| <= {tol:.0%} wherever gain > 0; HSC honest cost <= {vg['hsc_tol']:.0%}")
    print("  rule set = C cap / verify-down / D auction")
    print(f"  {'rule set':<26} | worst best-response gain over lambda (lambda, strategy)"
          f"{'':<26}| BRG  | HSC extra cost (two shocks) | HSC  | SPT/SST (conflicts at worst lambda)")
    verdict = {}
    for rule in rules:
        rs = [search[f'{rule}|{lam}'] for lam in vg['lambda_vals']]
        worst = max(rs, key=lambda r_: r_['best']['gain'])
        costs = g2[rule]
        g2_pass = all(abs(v_) <= vg['hsc_tol'] for v_ in costs.values())
        verdict[rule] = {'BRG': all(r_['BRG_pass'] for r_ in rs), 'HSC': g2_pass,
                         'SPT': all(r_['SPT_pass'] for r_ in rs), 'SST': all(r_['SST_pass'] for r_ in rs),
                         'SPT_by_rho': {k_: all(r_['spt_by_rho'][k_]['pass'] for r_ in rs) for k_ in rs[0]['spt_by_rho']},
                         'worst_best_response_gain': worst['best']['gain'],
                         'worst_lambda': worst['lambda'], 'worst_strategy': worst['best']['label'],
                         'max_conflicts': max(r_['n_conflict'] for r_ in rs), 'HSC_cost': costs}
        cs = list(costs.values())
        print(f"  {rule:<26} | {worst['best']['gain']:+7.2%} ({worst['lambda']:.0%}, {worst['best']['label'][:38]:<38}) | "
              f"{'pass' if verdict[rule]['BRG'] else 'FAIL'} | {cs[0]:+7.3%} / {cs[1]:+7.3%} | "
              f"{'pass' if g2_pass else 'FAIL'} | {'pass' if verdict[rule]['SPT'] else 'FAIL'}/{'pass' if verdict[rule]['SST'] else 'FAIL'} ({verdict[rule]['max_conflicts']})")
    print('  BRG / SPT / SST by lambda (lambda = odds per year that a private company is auctioned / lists):')
    print(f"  {'rule set':<26} | " + ' | '.join(f'{lam:>9.0%}' for lam in vg['lambda_vals']))
    for rule in rules:
        cells = []
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            r_ = search[f'{rule}|{lam}']
            cells.append(f"{r_['best']['gain']:+6.1%} {'BRG' if r_['BRG_pass'] else '---'} {'SPT' if r_['SPT_pass'] else '---'} {'SST' if r_['SST_pass'] else '---'}")
        print(f"  {rule:<26} | " + ' | '.join(cells))
    growth_surf = _p5_growth_surface(p, vg['surface_rules'], strategies)
    dmg = _p5_dmg(p, vg['dmg_rules'], strategies)
    uos = _p5_direction(p, vg['dmg_rules'], [0.0, lam_base], strategies)
    for k_, c_ in uos.items():
        print(f"  UOS {c_['rule']} lambda {c_['lambda']:.0%} C share {c_['c_share']:.0%}: best gain " +
              ', '.join(f"{d}: {b['gain']:+.2%}" for d, b in sorted(c_['best'].items())))
    hec = _p5_hec(p, vg['dmg_rules'], [0.0, lam_base])
    for k_, c_ in hec.items():
        if c_['sigma'] > 0.0:
            print(f"  HEC {c_['rule']} lambda {c_['lambda']:.0%} sigma {c_['sigma']:.0%}: gain mean {c_['gain_mean']:+.2%} "
                  f"[{c_['gain_p05']:+.2%}, {c_['gain_p95']:+.2%}], share gaining {c_['share_gaining']:.0%}, "
                  f"state stake mean {c_['state_mean']:+.2%}")
    for rule, d_ in dmg.items():
        print(f"  DMG {rule}: {d_['n_dominant']} of {d_['n_strategies']} strategies gain in all {d_['n_scenarios']} scenarios ({d_['n_dominant_material']} by more than {d_['material_threshold']:.0%}); "
              f"maximin {d_['maximin']['min_gain']:+.2%} ({d_['maximin']['label']}); "
              f"largest share of scenarios gaining {d_['max_share_gaining']:.0%}")
    for rule, by_g in growth_surf.items():
        print(f"  best-response gain by growth g (rows) and lambda (columns), {rule}:")
        print(f"    {'g':>7} | " + ' | '.join(f'{lam:>11.0%}' for lam in vg['lambda_vals']) + ' | honest TW')
        for g_, cell in by_g.items():
            row = ' | '.join(
                f"{c['gain']:+6.1%} {'BRG' if c['BRG'] else '---'} {'SPT' if c['SPT'] else '---'} {'SST' if c['SST'] else '---'}"
                for c in cell['by_lambda'].values())
            print(f"    {float(g_):>7.2%} | {row} | £{cell['honest_TW_m']:,.0f}m")
    for rule in (_BASE_RULE, _CANDIDATE_RULE):
        if rule not in rules:
            continue
        print(f"  best response by lambda, {rule}:")
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            r_ = search[f'{rule}|{lam}']
            print(f"    lambda {lam:>4.0%}: {r_['best']['gain']:+7.2%} {r_['best']['label']}   "
                  f"(gain>0: {r_['n_gaining']}, SPT/SST conflicts: {r_['n_conflict_spt']}/{r_['n_conflict_sst']})")
    for rule in (_BASE_RULE, _CANDIDATE_RULE):
        if rule in rules:
            print(f"  best strategy by family, {rule}, lambda {lam_base:.0%}:")
            for fam_, r_ in search[f'{rule}|{lam_base}']['best_by_family'].items():
                print(f"    {fam_:<22} {r_['gain']:+7.2%}  ({r_['label']})")

    # strategy-free ceiling on the gain, checked against every best response
    tw_free = _p5_no_tax_tw(p)
    bound = {}
    for rule in rules:
        for lam in vg['lambda_vals']:
            bound[f'{rule}|{lam}'] = _p5_upper_bound(p, rule, lam, tw_free)
            if search[f'{rule}|{lam}']['best']['gain'] > bound[f'{rule}|{lam}'] + 1e-9:
                raise AssertionError(f'VALIDATION FAILED: best response exceeds the no-tax ceiling at {rule}|{lam}')
    cand0, candb = f'{_CANDIDATE_RULE}|0.0', f'{_CANDIDATE_RULE}|{vg["lambda_base"]}'
    print(f"  ceiling (no declaration strategy can beat a no-tax run): a no-tax family ends "
          f"{bound[cand0]:+.1%} above the honest one (loose: it includes the tax on A/B); best response captures "
          f"{search[cand0]['best']['gain'] / bound[cand0]:.0%} of it at lambda 0 and "
          f"{search[candb]['best']['gain'] / bound[candb]:.0%} at lambda {vg['lambda_base']:.0%}"
          f" ({_CANDIDATE_RULE})")
    conv = _p5_conventional(p, sorted(set(sw['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext'] + vg['conv_extra_alphas'])))
    print(f"  conventional self-declared wealth tax (flat {conv['rate']:.3%} on declared value, "
          f"same honest burden as the WDT): best response {conv['best']['gain']:+.1%} at "
          f"(alpha_C|alpha_D) = {conv['best']['key']}; full understatement {conv['full_understatement_gain']:+.1%}")
    print('    gain by alpha (alpha_C = alpha_D): ' + ', '.join(
        f'{a}: {g_:+.1%}' for a, g_ in conv['diag_alpha'].items()))
    print(f"    WDT {_CANDIDATE_RULE}: best response {search[cand0]['best']['gain']:+.1%} (lambda 0), "
          f"{search[candb]['best']['gain']:+.1%} (lambda {vg['lambda_base']:.0%})")

    head_rules = vg['headline_rules']
    head_lams = [0.0, lam_base]
    headline = _p5_headline(p, head_rules, head_lams)
    # consistency with the library of record: at ratios the library holds, the slice is a subset, so it cannot beat the library best
    lib_grid = set(sw['alpha_vals'] + vg['alpha_ext'])   # the library only holds these ratios
    worst_over = -1.0
    for rule in head_rules:
        for lam in head_lams:
            lib = search[f'{rule}|{lam}']['best']['gain']
            worst_over = max(worst_over, max(c['gain'] for a_, c in headline[rule][str(lam)].items()
                                   if c['gain'] is not None and float(a_) in lib_grid) - lib)
    validation['checks']['headline_slice_never_beats_library_best'] = {
        'ok': worst_over <= 1e-12, 'detail': f'max(slice best - library best)={worst_over:.2e}'}
    if worst_over > 1e-12:
        raise AssertionError('VALIDATION FAILED: headline_slice_never_beats_library_best')
    print(f"  PASS  headline_slice_never_beats_library_best max(slice - library)={worst_over:.2e}")
    for rule in head_rules:
        print(f"  HLC best response by alpha, {rule}, lambda {lam_base:.0%}: " + ', '.join(
            f"{a}: {c['gain']:+.1%}" for a, c in headline[rule][str(lam_base)].items() if c['gain'] is not None))

    for key, r_ in search.items():
        if r_['lambda'] not in (0.0, lam_base):
            r_['all'] = sorted(r_['all'], key=lambda x: -x['gain'])[:25]

    data = {
        'meta': {
            'code': 'VALGEN', 'generated': date.today().isoformat(),
            'model_version': 'valgen P5 (four routes, verification hazard, corrective auction on C and D, declaration strategies, rule sets; ledger)',
            'N_val': N, 'bridge_series': bridge['historical_series'],
            'params': {'tau_0': p['tau_0'], 'tau_m': p['tau_m'], 'k': p['k'],
                       'W_min': p['W_min'], 'V0_m': p['V0_m'], 'g': g, 'rho': p['rho'],
                       'index_rate': ir, 'rate_scenario': p.get('rate_scenario'), 'val_basis': p.get('val_basis', 'legacy_nominal'), 'val_basis_info': p.get('val_basis_info'), 'rho_sens': p.get('rho_sens'),
                       'schedule': p.get('schedule', 'logistic'), 'ladder': p.get('ladder'),
                       **{k: v for k, v in vg.items() if k not in _RETIRED_KEYS}},
            'validation': validation,
        },
        'bridge': bridge,
        'life': life,
        'examples': examples,
        'pairs_at_N_val': {'N': N, 'g': g, 'rho': p['rho'], 'by_alpha': pairs},
        'p2_benchmark_plan_s1': p2_data['plan_s1'],
        'p2_plan_fixture_applies': p2_data['plan_fixture_applies'],
        'p2b_oscillation': p2b_info['oscillation'],
        'p2b_round_trip_units': p2b_info['round_trip_units'],
        'p2b_family_grid': {'T': vg['T'], 'G': vg['G'], 'g': g, 'rho': p['rho'],
                            'index_rate': ir, 'state_tol': tol,
                            'metric_notes': {
                                'gain': 'f_T(a)/f_T(1) - 1; + = family ends with more',
                                'state_stake_rel': 's_T(a)/s_T(1) - 1',
                                'pv_rel': '(PV(a)-PV(1))/PV(1), PV of true value received at rho',
                                'alignment': 'conflict = gain > 0 and |pv_rel| > state_tol'},
                            'by_switches': grid},
        'p3_surface': {'T': vg['T'], 'G': vg['G'], 'g': g, 'rho': p['rho'], 'index_rate': ir,
                       'state_tol': tol, 'shares': shares,
                       'consumption': vg['consumption'], 'TW_honest': honest3['family_true_T'],
                       'metric_notes': {
                           'gain': 'TW(a)/TW(1) - 1; TW = family true net worth at T',
                           'pv_rel': '(PV(a)-PV(1))/PV(1), PV of true value received at rho',
                           'key': 'alpha_C|alpha_D'},
                       'cells': surface, 'conflict_cells': conflicts},
        'p3_reset_sensitivity': sens,
        'p3_dilution': p3_info['dilution_gain_by_C_share'],
        'p4_lambda_sweep': {'lambda_base': lam_base, 'verified_threshold': thr,
                            'metric_notes': {
                                'by_alpha_C': 'alpha_D = 1; gain and pv_rel vs the honest family at the same lambda',
                                'surface': 'key alpha_C|alpha_D',
                                'verified_share': 'share of Route C units (family + state) verified, by year'},
                            'by_lambda': lam_sweep},
        'p4_C_heavy_stress_gain': p4_info['C_heavy_gain_by_lambda_alpha_C_0.5'],
        'p5': {'thresholds': {'brg_tol': vg['brg_tol'], 'hsc_tol': vg['hsc_tol'], 'state_tol': tol},
               'rules': rules, 'lambda_vals': vg['lambda_vals'], 'n_strategies': len(strategies),
               'shock_year': vg['shock_year'], 'g2_honest_shock_cost': g2,
               'verdict_by_rule': verdict, 'search': search, 'g2_honest_shock_detail': {r: v[1] for r, v in g2_full.items()},
               'no_tax_ceiling': {'TW_no_tax': tw_free, 'gain_ceiling_by_rule_lambda': bound},
               'conventional_baseline': conv,
               'headline': {'alphas': _headline_alphas(p), 'rules': head_rules, 'lambda_vals': head_lams,
                            'by_rule': headline,
                            'note': 'best response at each declaration ratio: max gain over strategies '
                                    'deviating at exactly that ratio; lower bound; alpha = 1 honest'},
               'growth_surface': {'note': 'best-response gain by g and lambda; growth and lambda are '
                                          'independent inputs; gain is a share of honest terminal wealth',
                                  'growth_vals': vg['growth_vals'], 'by_rule': growth_surf},
               'dmg': {'note': 'dominance grid: a strategy dominates if its gain over honest is positive in every '
                               'scenario (growth x lambda, market fall x lambda); lower bound over the library',
                       'by_rule': dmg},
               'uos': {'note': 'best gain by direction of deviation (under, over, mixed) and Route C share; A absorbs the share change',
                       'c_share_vals': vg['c_share_vals'], 'cells': uos},
               'hec': {'note': 'honest valuation error on Routes C and D, multiplicative lognormal AR(1), '
                               'error-free honest as reference; gain < 0 is the cost of honest error',
                       'sigmas': vg['hec_sigmas'], 'paths': vg['hec_paths'], 'phi': vg['hec_phi'],
                       'phi_C': vg.get('hec_phi_C', vg['hec_phi']), 'phi_D': vg.get('hec_phi_D', vg['hec_phi']),
                       'seed': vg['hec_seed'], 'cells': hec},
               'notes': {'BRG': 'best-response gain over the strategy library <= brg_tol',
                         'SPT': 'every strategy with gain > 0 has |pv_rel| <= state_tol',
                         'SST': 'every strategy with gain > 0 has |state_rel| <= state_tol',
                         'HSC': 'honest family, genuine market fall: terminal net worth vs the baseline rule set (units cap, no auction)'}},
        'p4_C_share_sensitivity': {'alpha_D': 1.0, 'lambda_base': lam_base, 'cells': c_sens,
                                   'note': 'A absorbs the change in C share; alpha_C grid includes alpha_ext'},
    }
    data['p6'] = p6_out
    print('[9b] lambda_C x lambda_D grid, V0 band sweep, HLC pair...')
    data['p3_lambda_grid'] = _p3_lambda_grid(p, strategies)
    data['v0_sweep'] = _v0_sweep(p, strategies)
    data['p5']['hlc_pair'] = _hlc_pair(p)
    print('[9c] JST replay (D1a) and the rho sensitivity (D1c)...')
    data['replay'] = _p7_replay(p, strategies)
    data['rho'] = {'base': p['rho'], 'sweep': p['rho_sens'],
                   'note': 'SST (state terminal stake) is the primary state test and does not depend on rho; SPT is the sensitivity',
                   'spt_by_rho': {k_: v_['spt_by_rho'] for k_, v_ in search.items()},
                   'verdict_spt_by_rho': {rule: verdict[rule]['SPT_by_rho'] for rule in rules}}
    for rule in vg['headline_rules']:
        if rule in verdict:
            print(f"  state tests, {rule}: SST (primary) {'pass' if verdict[rule]['SST'] else 'FAIL'}; SPT by rho " +
                  ', '.join(f"{k_}: {'pass' if v_ else 'FAIL'}" for k_, v_ in verdict[rule]['SPT_by_rho'].items()))
    assert all('|' in k for k in data['p3_surface']['cells']), 'p3_surface.cells overwritten'
    ensure_dir(_OUT)
    with open(_JSON_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as fh:
        json.dump(_clean(data), fh, indent=2, allow_nan=False)
    print(f"\nWritten: {_JSON_PATH}  ({_JSON_PATH.stat().st_size / 1024:.0f} KB)")


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main(dry_run='--dry-run' in sys.argv)
